(as the request states it) | Where stated |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:51:**[52] Operation units (stated in `operation`):**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:59:## 2-old. The rules as first written (superseded by the revision above)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:78:## 3. The wire schema, word for word (examples from no covered company, AGENTS §6)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:80:**[52] These descriptions replace the ones in the table below:**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:82:| Field | Description [52] |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:93:**[52] The family header is rendered from the family's data** (no member id is fixed in code):\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:143:## 4. Build\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:162:## 5. The $0 blind test (registered; REPAIR-DESIGN.md §5 with rounds 51's fixes)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:215:**[52] Additions to Part A.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244:**[52] Readers.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:248:  - any of D737's five defects;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7:## D1 · 2026-10-15 · Input classification carries each input's related companies\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:20:## D2 · 2026-10-15 · Config holds only the choices a person makes\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:38:## D3 · 2026-10-15 · Config has no budget or concurrency limits\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:45:## D4 · 2026-10-15 · Dispatch is by tag only, never by company\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:57:## D5 · 2026-10-15 · Time is the material's own time and the run's day\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:75:## D6 · 2026-10-15 · The research universe is its own module\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:88:## D7 · 2026-10-15 · No input store; replay is a test database, not a design concern\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:111:## D8 · 2026-10-16 · Classification's lookup tables: one data file, results are tags\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:127:## D9 · 2026-10-16 · A day is cut in New York time; only the day counts\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:141:## D10 · 2026-10-16 · The system starts at a stream of classified items\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:162:## D11 · 2026-10-16 · Related objects and the theme library\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:179:## D12 · 2026-10-16 · No current-day clock in the system\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:194:## D13 · 2026-10-16 · The system is driven by information, not by the calendar\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:206:## D14 · 2026-10-16 · Two modes, designed apart: stream and pull\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:221:## D15 · 2026-10-16 · Macro, political and economic material in the classification\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:245:## D16 · 2026-10-16 · A human review pool for what the tables do not know\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:266:## D17 · 2026-10-16 · Receive is merged into dispatch\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:277:## D18 · 2026-10-16 · One switch: the universe decides what is processed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:298:## D19 · 2026-10-16 · Freeze v1: everything up to classification\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:342:## D20 · 2026-10-16 · A PRD per module, in Markdown, viewable from the design page\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:364:## D21 · 2026-10-16 · Any change refreshes everything, by one command\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:380:## D22 · 2026-10-16 · Refreshing is a reasoning pass; the script only checks\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:405:## D23 · 2026-10-16 · Tables without XBRL tags are read by the model\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:433:## D24 · 2026-10-16 · Financial reports are not streamed; pull mode reads them when a thesis needs them\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:468:## D25 · 2026-10-16 · One extraction module, read by category from a senior hedge fund analyst's view\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:502:## D26 · 2026-10-18 · The views database is the system's core\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:533:## D27 · 2026-10-18 · Extraction reads the whole item by category, then matches it against the drivers\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:567:## D28 · 2026-10-18 · Financial reports stream again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:576:## D29 · 2026-10-18 · A final verdict before any view is closed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:598:## D30 · 2026-10-18 · Conflicting sources and the consensus\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:616:## D31 · 2026-10-18 · Order, one writer, and the link between the levels\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:646:## D32 · 2026-10-18 · Table data comes one release at a time; XBRL is not pushed again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:665:## D33 · 2026-10-18 · Extraction only reads; matching and writing belong to the views database\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:680:## D34 · 2026-10-18 · An SEC filing is dated by the day SEC makes it public\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:695:## D35 · 2026-10-18 · Extraction v1 is final\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:716:## D36 · 2026-10-18 · One word per concept in the input and extraction modules\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:741:## D37 · 2026-10-18 · Freeze v1 of the input side and extraction\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:753:## D38 · 2026-10-20 · The views database rebuilt: a view is a question with a five-rung ladder and a due date\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:823:## D39 · 2026-10-20 · Writing into the views database: match by where a candidate belongs, then one round of re-judging\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:869:## D40 · 2026-10-20 · The matching judge: a general model first, every match recorded, humans label, a small model later\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:899:## D41 · 2026-10-20 · What the rebuilt views database changes outside it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:937:## D42 · 2026-10-20 · Extraction hands over evidence and candidate views as two things; evidence is matched to what its view already holds\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:990:## D43 · 2026-10-20 · A second stable version of the design is sealed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1002:## D44 · 2026-10-20 · Matching is the model's alone: no key matched by code\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1027:## D45 · 2026-10-20 · Only what Alex said or decided is decided; Claude's proposals are listed apart\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1064:## D46 · 2026-10-20 · Alex decides Claude's views proposals one by one\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1150:## D47 · 2026-10-20 · End-to-end consistency from the universe to the views database\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1197:## D48 · 2026-10-20 · The views database, with match labelling, is frozen as version 1\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1215:## D49 · 2026-10-20 · Code review of the frozen views database: contradictions fixed, no new mechanism\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1241:## D50 · 2026-10-20 · Clean-up after the freeze\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1256:## D51 · 2026-10-21 · Claude's open items settled: one re-judging rule, dependencies chosen in the matching call, no consensus\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1316:## D52 · 2026-10-21 · Plain, consistent wording across the design page and PRDs\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1350:## D53 · 2026-10-21 · A full line-by-line read of the page and PRDs, in rounds\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1408:## D54 · 2026-10-21 · A view's state is frozen at its due date; pull mode runs at the end of the day\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1449:## D55 · 2026-10-22 · The final verdict checked against the rebuilt views database; a removed object's views stop updating\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1477:## D56 · 2026-10-22 · A full sweep before sealing v12\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1506:## D57 · 2026-10-22 · A view has one switch: open or closed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1534:## D58 · 2026-10-22 · A deep review before freezing everything but pull mode\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1596:## D59 · 2026-10-22 · How a candidate view names its object; a view from Alex's own memo\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1619:## D60 · 2026-10-22 · The deep review again, after D59\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1653:## D61 · 2026-10-22 · Clean-up: a code review, bloat removed, superseded seals out of the tree\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1676:## D62 · 2026-10-23 · The POC build: Alex's choices, in his words\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1685:## D63 · 2026-10-24 · Re-judging once a day; the first window ends on 2026-08-15\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md: