at the standard keeps\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2915:## D241 · 2026-10-29 · One unified definition of the ledger's types, question opening and evidence levels, with a traced golden set, before more prompt work\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2920:## D242 · 2026-10-29 · The standard becomes a web page, the extraction step's PRD; AGENTS.md and the README are cleaned and carry the prompt, measuring and iterating principles\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2925:## D243 · 2026-10-29 · The extraction standard is signed: proposal 5 stricter, the other eleven at their leans; lean cautious, catch the increment\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2932:## D244 · 2026-10-29 · Claude sets the dev/test split; scores are leads and Claude reads the traces every time; first the role-v29 baseline\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2937:## D245 · 2026-10-30 · role-v42 (`poc-v58`) is the extraction request; its must-not questions on small release dates are the next class\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2943:## D246 · 2026-10-30 · role-v51 (`poc-v67`) is the extraction request\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2948:## D247 · 2026-10-30 · role-v53 (`poc-v69`) is the extraction request: the attribution fields are defined in the schema\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2954:## D248 · 2026-10-30 · What counts as one question and one piece of evidence: seven boundaries, chosen one by one\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2969:## D249 · 2026-10-30 · A test the model applies to each statement is a check at the end of the same request; role-v63 (`poc-v79`) measured, the default stays role-v53\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2976:## D250 · 2026-10-31 · Four evidence boundaries and the counting unit settled; the ruler is fixed before any further measurement (standard version 5)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2988:## D251 · 2026-10-31 · The extraction request may read the open questions as a daily snapshot (architecture under test)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2993:## D252 · 2026-10-31 · The extraction prompt teaches what noise looks like, with general paired counter-examples; useful theses and evidence mus