, not core versus supporting\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4023:## D373 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Continue scoring when gold is disputed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027:## D374 · 2026-11-05 · Remove the misleading sampling setting\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4031:## 2026-11-05 · Incomplete thesis details do not block admission\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4035:## D375 · 2026-11-05 · Read the latest committed research library before each item\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4041:## D376 · 2026-11-05 · Remove the evidence reader's size rejection\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4045:## D377 · 2026-11-05 · Remove the question-catalog size rejection\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4049:## D378 · 2026-11-06 · The split extraction is sealed as a failed experiment; its useful lessons become production experiments (PRD 11)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4075:## D379 · 2026-11-06 · The current version is sealed; Alex re-plans the system design\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4093:## D380 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 runs on K6b with DeepSeek Flash; a format failure is retried once\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4101:## D381 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 2: a repeat joins only the group it is most like; three acceptance lines\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4107:## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4113:## D383 · 2026-11-08 · D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4119:## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4126:## D385 · 2026-11-08 · Target prices and valuation conclusions are not kept\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4133:## D386 · 2026-11-08 · Acceptance on fresh articles read by readers against the source\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4142:## D387 · 2026-11-09 · Clean Step 1 adopts c8; the PRD carries its system prompt, closing check and schema\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4172:## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4185:## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4204:## D390 · 2026-11-09 · A plan counts as undertaken once a deal under it is reported signed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4221:## D391 · 2026-11-09 · Close clean Step 1 on c8; state each change's effect on the judgement first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4238:## D392 · 2026-11-09 · A seeded end-to-end diagnostic of the clean system, all three stages approved\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4258:## D393 · 2026-11-09 · After Stage 2 of D392, fix capital spending (q12) first; c8 may change for it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4277:## D394 · 2026-11-10 · Capital spending (q12) is a known gap; the unseeded measurement starts\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4295:## D395 · 2026-11-10 · Run the unseeded clean measurement, three draws, graded on the seven must-open questions\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4311:## D396 · 2026-11-10 · Design the clean system's own judging step (Step 4)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4326:## D397 · 2026-11-10 · A topic that asks more than one thing gets one judged question; the other parts are shown as not judged\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4345:## D398 · 2026-11-10 · The clean ladder step carries D186: ranges against the reference, the favourable end registered, labels by code\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4365:## D399 · 2026-11-10 · The ladder request may teach how to build an event's five states\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4376:## D400 · 2026-11-10 · Stage A is read against absolute lines, with no paid control arm\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4391:## D401 · 2026-11-10 · Once a review finds nothing serious, build the ladder step and run Stage A without asking again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4400:## D402 · 2026-11-10 · Before more review or the build: send the ladder request once on six stored theses, for a few cents\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4414:## D403 · 2026-11-10 · An event's due day is a stated date or the last day of the thesis's period; the model picks no other day\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4428:## D404 · 2026-11-10 · After the probe: change the request for its three classes, send the same six again, then build\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4441:## D405 · 2026-11-10 · A reference's words must be the article's own, in one unbroken passage; otherwise the answer is sent back once\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4456:## D406 · 2026-11-10 · The two rules that kept slipping go into the answer's shape; then a probe that counts; then the build\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4469:## D407 · 2026-11-10 · One last probe of the ladder request, then the build, whichever way it comes out\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4484:## D408 · 2026-11-10 · Stage A missed its lines: stay at the ladder step, fix the event answers first, validate at no cost, then run the same Stage A once more\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4502:## D409 · 2026-11-10 · An event is answered in three outcomes: it happened, it is ruled out, or neither by the due day\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4519:## D410 · 2026-11-10 · A group named in a judged question and not listed member by member is not a fault of the question\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4530:## D411 · 2026-11-10 · An amount already reported may be the baseline of a ladder, labelled as that and never as the market's expectation\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4541:## D412 · 2026-11-10 · Every round is reflected on in the council to a recorded consensus, then the next test goes straight ahead; every trace is read by Claude itself\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4554:## D413 · 2026-11-10 · Where the texts do not settle it, an amount the company owes or guarantees is registered with the lower end favourable\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4568:## D414 · 2026-11-10 · Code sets the due day of a year's figure whose day is an estimate\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4581:## D415 · 2026-11-10 · The third Stage A is sent without asking again once each change is proved small and reviewed; a failure stops and goes to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4593:## D416 · 2026-11-10 · The lines stay; the ruling out of an event as a typed answer is proved small before anything else\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4606:## D417 · 2026-11-10 · A figure for a rolling twelve months with no publication day in the texts is declined\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4616:## D418 · 2026-11-10 · A government's permission or ban on a class of product belongs to the theme, not to the company\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4627:## D419 · 2026-11-10 · The fourth Stage A is sent without asking again once each change is proved small and reviewed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4638:## D420 · 2026-11-10 · A proceeding that formally ends without the conclusion the question asks for is ruled out; the question stays\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4650:## D421 · 2026-11-10 · Each further change is tested alone; all passing, the fourth Stage A is sent without asking again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4663:## D422 · 2026-11-10 · A second look by the model at its own answer is tested small, as a candidate; adoption is Alex's after the result\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4677:## D423 · 2026-11-10 · Work on Jev's revision relation stops; \"a later version does not take the older record's questions\" is accepted as a direction and, once measured, withdrawn by its author; the rule stays, pending Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4698:## D424 · 2026-11-10 · The writer keeps giving a \"later version\" the older record's questions; the fix is closed without a change\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4711:## D425 · 2026-11-10 · The second look is not adopted\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4721:## D426 · 2026-11-10 · The ladder step is not tuned further on the 44 theses; the preparation of Stage B opens on the step as it ran in the fourth Stage A, its $0 baseline reading first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4738:## D427 · 2026-11-11 · Clean Step 2 is closed and frozen; it goes to production only with the whole clean path\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4756:## D428 · 2026-11-11 · Stage B's lines compare figure and yes/no questions apart with the baseline\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4771:## D429 · 2026-11-11 · The adapter's ladder mode is built; once a review finds nothing serious, Stage B is sent without asking again\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4784:## D430 · 2026-11-12 · A figure control's due day counts as the ruler's when both mark the same publication\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795:## D431 · 2026-11-12 · The clean path is compared end to end with production as it now runs, with no preset questions on either side\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4806:## D432 · 2026-11-12 · After Stage B, the next phase is how Step 1 cuts a matter into theses\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4817:## D433 · 2026-11-12 · Open Step 1 version c14: D38's year boundary in the two merge sentences, tested small first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4831:## D434 · 2026-11-13 · After c14's failed stage 1: finish diagnosing Step 1's other defects, then change them together\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4839:## D435 · 2026-11-13 · Run gate 1 of the combined Step 1 plan: three small proofs on stored data\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4847:## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4857:## D437 · 2026-11-13 · Carry changes 1 and 2 to gate 2 although the year line was missed\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4865:## D438 · 2026-11-13 · Send gate 2\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4879:## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4885:## D441 · 2026-11-13 · The memory diagnostic does not let c15yc go on: the year change stops, c8 stays (rule fixed by council consensus, D440)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4891:## D442 · 2026-11-13 · Next step: D431's same-day end-to-end comparison, run as a diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4897:## D443 · 2026-11-13 · Shape B': an exploratory census of final-answer losses, the stored clean chain against fresh production v118 draws (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4902:## D444 · 2026-11-13 · Three fresh production draws under a corrected ledger, replacing the stopped ones (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4908:## D445 · 2026-11-13 · Next: a $0 source-to-answer trace of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses, memory first (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4913:## D446 · 2026-11-13 · A $0 audit of a narrow typed-unit contract on the stored losses and correct controls (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4918:## D447 · 2026-11-13 · The typed-unit line stops; next a reviewed $0 design for wiring the ladder step end to end and its diagnostic same-day run (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4923:## D448 · 2026-11-13 · The wiring contract is settled; build and prove at $0, then review the code (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4928:## D449 · 2026-11-13 · The wiring's code review: four structural rules, two changes to the run states (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4967:## D450 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the slice: one fresh day through the wired path, live, on its own $1.50 ledger (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4984:## D451 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the full run: three clean draws and three production draws, same day, ledger $14.84 (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4999:## D452 · 2026-11-13 · The reading plan for the full run (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5013:## D453 · 2026-11-13 · Redo c2's Step 1 (a dropped response; council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5022:## D454 · 2026-11-13 · After the census and Stage A of the full run: the readings continue in the agreed order (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5037:## D455 · 2026-11-13 · Stage B's judgement reading stops for the full run: line 3 is unexercised under every treatment (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5054:## D456 · 2026-11-13 · The next angle: trace production's kept-but-unlinked facts at $0, beside the clean path's (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5070:## D457 · 2026-11-13 · Production's unlinked facts cost no final answer in this window; next a $0 review of the opening losses (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5090:## D458 · 2026-11-13 · No opening phase on the review's evidence; next a $0 trace of Stage A's agreed failures (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5111:## D459 · 2026-11-13 · Stage A's first-pass faults form no class; next the standard's tests on the three unsettled opening classes and a bounded model-account diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5130:## D460 · 2026-11-13 · Next a whole-request $0 prompt audit of clean Step 1 (c8), identity first (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5151:## D461 · 2026-11-13 · The prompt audit's result; the date contradiction (F6) is designed and falsified first, the identity lever deferred (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5166:## D462 · 2026-11-13 · F6 is recorded as a contradiction with uncertain standalone effect; the status report for Alex comes before the identity comparison (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5181:## D463 · 2026-11-13 · The identity lever: a general prompt clause first (P), written and probe-designed before any send (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5201:## D464 · 2026-11-13 · Send the case-specific identity diagnostic, c16 version 5 against c8, under one $5 ledger (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5219:## D465 · 2026-11-13 · The identity diagnostic: the year boundary moved its error; the line stops; c8 stays (council consensus; Alex active again)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5234:## D466 · 2026-11-13 · Deep reflection (Alex's request): stop circling, two choices for Alex, one in-scope measurement prepared at $0, new guard lines (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5260:## D467 · 2026-11-13 · The ladder-cost measurement is feasible only with four more $0 proofs; it goes to Alex as a candidate, not a send (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5271:## D468 · 2026-11-13 · The ladder-cost measurement stops at its $0 proofs; the forward work waits on Alex's two choices (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5286:## D469 · 2026-11-13 · Provisional choices while Alex has not answered; the ladder-step refusal fix starts with a $0 boundary check (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5297:## D470 · 2026-11-13 · The ladder-refusal candidate stops; the 41 Stage A splits are recorded, eight with a provisional reading from D414; Stage A's verdict is unchanged (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5311:## D471 · 2026-11-13 · The written-ladder line stands; the ten \"right only by refusal\" theses traced; one period-rule candidate (c17) probed on stored cases (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5327:## D472 · 2026-11-13 · A budget exception for the period probe: the nine never-sent jobs are sent before any answer is read (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5336:## D473 · 2026-11-13 · The period candidate c17 fails its frozen lines; Step 1 sentence changes on these articles stop (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5349:## D474 · 2026-11-13 · The unsigned-deal candidate c18 is probed on unseen articles against a stored library (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5362:## D475 · 2026-11-13 · c18 is not adopted: the unseen target is not moved; c8's own variance noted against D473's federal line (council round 18 pending)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5372:## D476 · 2026-11-13 · Next test: a $0 source check of the eleven first-pass refusals (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5384:## D477 · 2026-11-13 · Reflection rounds 19–22: Stage A not passed; no H100 or Step 1 change; production stays the default; the clean path's choices go to Alex (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5403:## D478 · 2026-11-13 · Under D439 the council takes D477's choice 2 and probes it: the first step writes each new thesis's settling figure or event and its fixed outcomes (c19)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5417:## D479 · 2026-11-13 · c19 fails; under D439 the council takes D477's choice 3: production stays the default and the next test comes from production's own losses\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5428:## D480 · 2026-11-13 · Under choice 3, production's opening rule is probed with a price (D191 point 4, D368 item 1) on its stored requests (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5441:## D481 · 2026-11-13 · The production price change fails and stops; next a $0 census of the opening losses by what the article states (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5453:## D482 · 2026-11-13 · No further paid test on this ruler today; production stays the default; the measured map goes to Alex (council consensus under D439)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5465:## D483 · 2026-11-14 · Deep reflection council (mw): the way to production is a use-oriented acceptance, prepared on stored runs first; to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5488:## D484 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens the use-oriented acceptance, trial run first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5497:## D485 · 2026-11-14 · The trial run's design (version 3) goes to the readers, with a stop rule for design rounds (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5506:## D486 · 2026-11-14 · The trial run's result, and the acceptance design that goes to Alex for his lines and budget (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5520:## D487 · 2026-11-14 · The lean path: step 1 builds nothing (the dates are the source's); step 2 runs one fresh week, slice first (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5530:## D488 · 2026-11-14 · Clean Step 1 resends a dropped connection, as production does (council consensus; root-caused in the lean step)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5546:## D489 · 2026-11-14 · The fresh week's result: not clear by the rule, no system chosen; the company's main numbers as questions goes to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5571:## D490 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a test: the new system may open questions on the company's revenue and margin\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5583:## D491 · 2026-11-14 · The revenue-and-margin test arm (c20) fails its probe's first step and is stopped; what next goes to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5603:## D492 · 2026-11-14 · Alex: a deep council review of the traces, then the next step to try; no circles, learn from the mistakes\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5615:## D493 · 2026-11-14 · Reflection council mx: no more sentences in the one call; next, a $0 test of the kept figures as a company record (council consensus under D492)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5641:## D494 · 2026-11-14 · The kept figures as a company record: close, not ready; who a figure is from is stored per statement; three choices to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5665:## D495 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a new version of the clean Step 1 record: each kept figure carries its own source and a fixed-form period\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5677:## D496 · 2026-11-14 · The figure-fields arm (c21): the fields repair attribution, the probe is undecided and stops; the arm infers what articles imply (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5696:## D497 · 2026-11-15 · Alex approves a second version of the figure fields and its probe\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5707:## D498 · 2026-11-15 · The figure fields, second version (c22): both faults of the first gone, the gain kept, not a pass by one figure (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5729:## D499 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: go straight to the record test on unread articles with the second version as it is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5741:## D500 · 2026-11-15 · The record test on unread articles: the two records are not separated; c22 is not adopted; one choice goes to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5765:## D501 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: test a financial record as something the product shows, $0 first\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5777:## D502 · 2026-11-15 · The table test: no wrong join found, the written answer line met, no saving of effort shown; the table goes to Alex as a tested mock (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5798:## D503 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: review the mock table and test it, at $0, on the fresh week's three missed matters\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5811:## D504 · 2026-11-15 · The table on the fresh week: one of three matters undecided, two not findable by the line; eleven of twelve key figures are in the table; one product question goes to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5835:## D505 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: the kept financial figures should reach the judgements of related questions; first a $0 check\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5848:## D506 · 2026-11-15 · The delivery check: one kept financial fact did not reach a question it bears on; six open leads; nothing is built on it (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5870:## D507 · 2026-11-15 · Alex: size the gap first, at $0, over everything the new system kept that week\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5881:## D508 · 2026-11-15 · The census of the class: three confirmed missing fact-and-question pairs in three of seven questions, 23 unresolved pairs; one test of the effect on a judgement is offered to Alex (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5902:## D509 · 2026-11-15 · Alex goes inactive: Claude operates by his rules, and every round's run is examined in depth with the council (D439 in force again)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5921:## D510 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the six-call test of one missing fact's effect on one stored judgement is sent (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5935:## D511 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the six-call test is inconclusive; no change and no further send on the delivery line; a cold reflection council comes next (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5952:## D512 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the reflection council's consensus: a decision page for Alex comes first; no further reading or send before it (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5969:## D513 · 2026-11-15 · Correction to D506 and D508: the new system does look back, but only at statements with no link\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5990:## D514 · 2026-11-15 · Correction to D513's wording of the look-back rule (found by the reflection council, round 4)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6005:## D515 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the decision page is the reflection council's outcome; nothing further is sent or run on the lean path until Alex answers it (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6023:## D516 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: D515's wait is superseded; the next step is a $0 sizing and design of the comparison, reviewed by the council before any send (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6043:## D517 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the comparison is sized and not sent; the next step is a side-by-side of the two systems' output on the fresh week, then a bounded council decision (council consensus)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6064:## D518 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the default and both systems stay (a bounded council decision); the side-by-side is corrected; the next investigation is a $0 census of unsupported judgements (council consensus, reflection round 8)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6083:## D519 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the side-by-side is left for Alex beside the decision page; the census of unsupported answers stands as corrected; four accounts are asked of the frozen judge, ceiling $0.10 (council consensus, reflection round 9)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6107:## D520 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the judge line stops at a note for Alex with nothing sent; the next step is a $0 trace of the old system's three agreed duplicate question pairs through their dated requests (council consensus, reflection rounds 10 and 11)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6132:## D521 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the duplicate-pair trace stands as corrected; the same-day candidates are traced against D375 at $0 (council consensus, reflection round 12)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6152:## D522 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the four-case visibility finding is kept as a lead; the proposed stored-request probe is not sent; first a $0 check of the historical inputs and the filing checks (council consensus, reflection round 13)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6170:## D523 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the reading-step probe is withdrawn; each duplicate's opening is traced to the comparison step at $0 (council consensus on the withdrawal, reflection round 14; the trace Claude's, to be reviewed)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6191:## D524 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the lean path is not closed; next a reviewed $0 design and deterministic proof of D375's per-article list (council consensus, reflection round 15)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6213:## D525 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the D375 proof's first design is not built; six revisions first (council consensus, reflection round 16)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6231:## D526 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the D375 proof's design is accepted for building once its recovery comparison is corrected; the unread lead does not come first (council consensus, reflection round 17)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6247:## D527 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the D375 proof's four stages are recorded as case-specific wiring findings; the registered proof has not passed; its missing checks are finished before any new version or paid measurement is considered (council consensus, reflection round 18)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6268:## D528 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the D375 proof needs row-level checks and required failure records before it is called passed; the measurement is to be designed 