easure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'} source guidance 108 None None None None e2715\nQUOTE 16 e2715 'Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.'\nfy27_q3_sequential_growth {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'sequential revenue growth', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3 versus Q2'} computed forecast 0.12266 None None growth ['fy27_q2_reported', 'fy27_q3_guidance'] None\nq3_guidance_beat_history {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'average revenue above guidance high end', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'past four quarters'} source third_party 0.031 None None None None e5089\nQUOTE 16 e5089 'Over the past four quarters, actual revenue has averaged 3.1% above the high end of guidance.'\nfy27_q3_external_estimate {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'} source third_party None None None None None e5088\nQUOTE 16 e5088 'However, I think Nvidia could report third-quarter revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion.'\nfy27_q3_forecast {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'} estimate forecast 113.6 None None None ['fy27_q3_guidance', 'q3_guidance_beat_history', 'fy27_q3_external_estimate'] None\nfy27_q4_forecast {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'} computed forecast 127.536 None None apply_growth ['fy27_q3_forecast', 'fy27_q3_sequential_growth'] None\nfy27_total_forecast {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'FY2027'} computed forecast 418.973 None None sum ['fy27_h1_reported', 'fy27_q3_forecast', 'fy27_q4_forecast'] None\n18 ('pair-old-3', 'separate-v35')\nf_ref_dc_fy27 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027'} source third_party 361 None None None None Morningstar estimates FY2027 Data Center revenue at $361 billion.\nf_dc_fy27_h1 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 first six months'} source reported 164 None None None None NVIDIA generated $164 billion in Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027.\nf_dc_fy27_q3 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q3'} source third_party 99.9 None None None None The cited analyst calculation holds Data Center at 92.5% of guided total revenue and gets $99.9 billion.\nf_dc_fy27_q4 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027 Q4'} estimate forecast 110 None None None ['f_dc_fy27_q3'] My estimate: about $110 billion, allowing for sequential growth from Q3 as hyperscale growth is expected to reaccelerate with Vera Rubin supply building.\nf_dc_fy27 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Data Center', 'period': 'FY2027'} computed forecast 373.9 None None sum ['f_dc_fy27_h1', 'f_dc_fy27_q3', 'f_dc_fy27_q4'] FY2027 estimate: reported first-half revenue plus estimated Q3 and Q4 revenue.\n20 ('single-O', 'single')\nf1 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'as of 2026-07-26'} source reported 25 None None None None NVIDIA reported $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\nf2 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments', 'scope': 'remainder of the fiscal year', 'period': 'FY2027'} source guidance 18 None None None None NVIDIA said it had $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year.\nf3 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'announced purchase of convertible bonds', 'scope': 'MediaTek', 'period': 'announced 2026-08-31'} source guidance 3.5 None None None None NVIDIA announced it would buy US$3.5 billion of MediaTek bonds convertible into shares.\nf4 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'equity investment commitments', 'scope': 'company', 'period': 'end of FY2027'} estimate forecast 46.5 None None None ['f1', 'f2', 'f3'] My estimate uses the reported $25 billion balance, the company-stated $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027, and the subsequently announced $3.5 billion MediaTek convertible-bond purchase. It assumes the latter two are incremental to the July balance and that a substantial portion remains relevant to commitments at FY2027 year-end.\n22 ('single-S', 'single')\nfig_consensus_2027 {'population': 'hyperscalers', 'measure': 'capital expenditures', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'} source consensus 1080 None None None None Bank of America reported analyst consensus for hyperscalers’ calendar 2027 spending.\nfig_nvidia_top_five_2027 {'population': 'top five hyperscalers', 'measure': 'capital expenditures', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'} source third_party 1300 None None None None NVIDIA said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\nfig_v6_forecast {'population': 'four largest AI hyperscalers', 'measure': 'data-center capex', 'scope': 'combined', 'period': 'CY2027'} estimate forecast 1110 None None None ['fig_consensus_2027', 'fig_nvidia_top_five_2027'] None\n24 ('single-E', 'single')\nf1 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2027'} source guidance 20 None None None None NVIDIA expects $20 billion in FY2027 CPU revenue; management also describes this as the FY2027 potential for Vera CPU.\nf2 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue growth multiplier', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028 relative to FY2027'} source guidance 2 None None None None Management said FY2028 Vera CPU revenue could be more than double the FY2027 potential.\nf3 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028'} computed guidance 40 None None product ['f1', 'f2'] None\nf4 {'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'scope': 'Vera CPU', 'period': 'FY2028'} estimate forecast 42 None None None None None\nQUOTE 26 e4273 'In fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, the growth rate moderated to 65%, while revenue reached $215.9 billion.'\nQUOTE 26 e3280 \"As if this weren't enough, Kress guided 70% growth for the full fiscal year, which was ahead of analyst estimates.\"\nQUOTE 32 e4704 'Three direct customers generated 44% ($78.2 billion) of Nvidia’s $177.8 billion revenue in the first half of fiscal 2027—up from two customers driving 35% a year earlier.'\nQUOTE 32 e74 'During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales. Revenues from the segment surged 92% year over year and grew 21% sequentially, driven by the rapid ramp-up of Blackwell 300 systems and robust networking demand.'\nQUOTE 32 e2517 'Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago'\nQUOTE 32 e4995 'The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027.'\nQUOTE 32 e3216 \"A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\"\nQUOTE 32 e2115 'Nvidia should generate well over $300 billion of data center revenue in calendar 2026, which is effectively fiscal 2027, and perhaps over $500 billion in fiscal 2028.'\nQUOTE 36 e3219 \"Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\"\nQUOTE 44 e2620 'These include equity investments of $99 billion and equity investment commitments of $25 billion as of July 26, 2026.'\nQUOTE 44 e2889 'The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.'\nQUOTE 44 e4486 'In late February, OpenAI announced $110 billion of new investment at a $730 billion pre-money valuation, including $30 billion each from Nvidia and SoftBank Group and $50 billion from Amazon.'\nQUOTE 48 e3660 'The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CPU revenue in its fiscal 2027, but expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028.'\nQUOTE 62 e4360 'For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.'\nQUOTE 62 e2295 'Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.'\nQUOTE 62 e4190 \"In the meantime, Nvidia's fiscal 2027 third-quarter guidance implies 12% sequential growth at the midpoint.\"\nQUOTE 62 e5360 'The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027.'\nQUOTE 62 e3453 \"A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\"\nQUOTE 62 e3455 \"Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\"\nQUOTE 64 e25 \"Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\"\nQUOTE 64 e5134 'Management projects revenues of around $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.'\nQUOTE 68 e3558 'The deal announced on Monday will see Nvidia buy bonds convertible into MediaTek shares.'\nQUOTE 68 e4669 'According to a Reuters exclusive , the chipmaker is weighing a US$10 billion commitment to the offering, serving as an early backer that could signal strong institutional confidence to public markets preparing to absorb the astronomical valuations and capital demands of frontier artificial intelligence labs.'\nQUOTE 70 e4756 \"Nvidia's own earnings call also highlighted the scale of the spending cycle. The company said the top five hyperscalers are expected to spend nearly $800 billion on capital expenditures in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\nA\"\nQUOTE 70 e4739 'before pushing that figure to $1.08 trillion in 2027.'\ndistinct source quotes used 49\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
