{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,re\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'','\\\\''src'\\\\'']\nimport paid_gate as p\nseen=set()\nfor i in p.build_plan('\\\\''v13s'\\\\''):\n for e,row in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items():\n  t=row['\\\\''text'\\\\'']; key=(i['\\\\''draw_store'\\\\''],e)\n  if key in seen:continue\n  seen.add(key)\n  if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\\"'$'\"\\\\n|\\\\bpercent\\\\b|\\\\d\\\\s*%\\\\s*(?:to|[-–—])\\\\s*[-−–]?\\\\d|\\\\d\\\\s*[xX×]\\\\b|(?:as much as|as low as|just over|just under|at most|no more than|or so|upwards of|only|approximately|roughly|not only)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$|'\"\\\\b(?:half|quarter)\\\\b.{0,50}\\\\\"'$'\"\\\\s*\\\\d.{0,28}[-–—]\\\\s*\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',t,re.I):\n   print(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],e,repr(t),repr(i['\\\\''shown'\\\\''][e]) if e=='\\\\''e2754'\\\\'' else '\\\\'''\\\\'')\nprint('\\\\''passages'\\\\'',len(seen))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,re\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'','\\\\''src'\\\\'']\nimport paid_gate as p\nseen=set()\nfor i in p.build_plan('\\\\''v13s'\\\\''):\n for e,row in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items():\n  t=row['\\\\''text'\\\\'']; key=(i['\\\\''draw_store'\\\\''],e)\n  if key in seen:continue\n  seen.add(key)\n  if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\\"'$'\"\\\\n|\\\\bpercent\\\\b|\\\\d\\\\s*%\\\\s*(?:to|[-–—])\\\\s*[-−–]?\\\\d|\\\\d\\\\s*[xX×]\\\\b|(?:as much as|as low as|just over|just under|at most|no more than|or so|upwards of|only|approximately|roughly|not only)\\\\s+\\\\\"'$|'\"\\\\b(?:half|quarter)\\\\b.{0,50}\\\\\"'$'\"\\\\s*\\\\d.{0,28}[-–—]\\\\s*\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',t,re.I):\n   print(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],e,repr(t),repr(i['\\\\''shown'\\\\''][e]) if e=='\\\\''e2754'\\\\'' else '\\\\'''\\\\'')\nprint('\\\\''passages'\\\\'',len(seen))'\"","aggregated_output":"pair-old-1 e1510 'The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027,' \npair-old-1 e3346 'For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.' \npair-old-1 e5056 'If that trend continues in the third quarter, revenue could reach roughly $113.6 billion, compared with the current high end of about $110.2 billion.' \npair-old-1 e5099 'Huang said roughly $400 billion in venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating jobs and massive demand for compute, which is subsequently driving demand for data centers.' \npair-old-1 e5142 \"Critical players like Oracle (NASDAQ: ORCL), now ubiquitous across cloud instances regardless of hyperscaler, saw backlogs grow to more than $650 billion, while neoclouds like Nebius (NASDAQ: NBIS) reported far larger increases, with Nebius's backlog up 4x.\" \npair-old-1 e5200 'The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June' \npair-old-1 e5226 \"about $58 billion in AI semiconductor revenue for fiscal 2026, up 186% from the prior year, followed by roughly $115 billion in fiscal 2027 and $230 billion in fiscal 2028, according to a Reuters report . Those are Broadcom's own projections, not outside analyst estimates.\" \npair-old-1 e5245 'The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.' \npair-old-1 e5263 'Huang also pointed to rising rental prices as evidence of tight demand. He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.' \npair-old-1 e5270 'According to research firm Gartner, neoclouds are expected to represent 20 percent of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030, underlining their competitiveness against hyperscalers.' \npair-old-1 e5304 'Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July. Gerstner said the companies need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end, up about 80% from his July estimate, \"just to keep the AI trade intact.\"' \npair-old-1 e5310 'That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.' \npair-old-1 e5326 'In the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, according to its latest annual report, revenue reached approximately $215.9 billion. This was a massive increase of nearly 65.5% compared with the prior year.' \npair-old-1 e5330 'However, AMD is testing FSR Multi Frame Generation of up to 8X in newer drivers for RDNA 4 GPUs (via VideoCardz), and that might arrive sooner than expected and give it an edge over DLSS 4.5.' \npair-old-1 e5331 'Early partners include the startup The Matrix, which is adopting NVLink Fusion for its next-generation Raptor XPU to connect Vera and NVLink Switch racks, building a complete NVLink 72 architecture that incorporates The Matrix chip. Amazon AWS and Annapurna Labs are also collaborating with us to integrate custom IP into the base die of NVHBM, unlocking 30% to 40% of computing resources on their cu' \npair-old-2 e1336 'The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027' \npair-old-2 e4061 \"Analysts expect Nvidia's revenue to land at $411 billion in fiscal 2027, an increase of almost 60x in a decade.\" \npair-old-2 e4377 'According to its latest annual report, in the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, revenue reached approximately $215.9 billion. This represents a 65.5% increase year over year, driven by intense demand for AI chips.' \npair-old-2 e4490 'Behind those projects, Huang said, sits roughly $100 billion of contracted customer demand.' \npair-old-2 e4801 'Huang said roughly $400 billion in venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating jobs and massive demand for compute, which is subsequently driving demand for data centers.' \npair-old-2 e4842 \"neoclouds like Nebius (NASDAQ: NBIS) reported far larger increases, with Nebius's backlog up 4x.\" \npair-old-2 e4898 'The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June' \npair-old-2 e4928 'The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.' \npair-old-2 e4935 'If we think of the Data Center Interconnect or the telecom market being sort of a 1x multiple, what we are seeing now for scale-across is probably 10x of what we saw for DCI. What we are seeing now for scale-out is probably 10x of what we are seeing for DCI. What we are seeing for scale-up, starting in the second half of 2027 for the first instance of CPO [co-packaged optics] going to scale-up, is' \npair-old-2 e4945 'He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.' \npair-old-2 e4954 'According to research firm Gartner, neoclouds are expected to represent 20 percent of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030, underlining their competitiveness against hyperscalers.' \npair-old-2 e4984 'Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July.' \npair-old-2 e4987 'He said stocks later consolidated after the $65 billion figure fell short of the roughly $75 billion investors had expected.' \npair-old-2 e4996 'That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.' \npair-old-2 e5015 'The forward GAAP price-to-earnings (P/E) of 21.96x sits nearly 58% below its 5-year average of 52.15x. Similarly, the forward price-to-sales (P/S) ratio of 12.82x is roughly 35% below its 5-year average of 19.79x.' \npair-old-3 e2754 'Revenue\\n$\\n96,221\\n$\\n46,743\\n$\\n177,837\\n$\\n90,805' '- e2754 [fact; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported revenue of $177.837 billion for the first six months of FY2027, versus $90.805 billion in the same period of FY2026.\\n    Quote: Revenue\\n$\\n96,221\\n$\\n46,743\\n$\\n177,837\\n$\\n90,805'\npair-old-3 e5127 'Huang said roughly $400 billion in venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating jobs and massive demand for compute, which is subsequently driving demand for data centers.' \npair-old-3 e5169 \"Critical players like Oracle (NASDAQ: ORCL), now ubiquitous across cloud instances regardless of hyperscaler, saw backlogs grow to more than $650 billion, while neoclouds like Nebius (NASDAQ: NBIS) reported far larger increases, with Nebius's backlog up 4x.\" \npair-old-3 e5229 \"A $2 trillion valuation would represent a substantial increase from Anthropic's $965 billion post-money valuation in May, when it raised $65 billion. Anthropic's annualized revenue run rate surpassed $65 billion by the end of July, up from about $9 billion at the end of 2025. The reported valuation also depends partly on the company's projections for approximately $190 billion to $200 billion in r\" \npair-old-3 e5241 'The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June' \npair-old-3 e5277 \"Management also outlined an aggressive runway: about $58 billion in AI semiconductor revenue for fiscal 2026, up 186% from the prior year, followed by roughly $115 billion in fiscal 2027 and $230 billion in fiscal 2028, according to a Reuters report . Those are Broadcom's own projections, not outside analyst estimates.\" \npair-old-3 e5281 'Broadcom expects AI semiconductor revenue to reach roughly $58 billion this year, then climb to about $115 billion in fiscal 2027 and $230 billion in fiscal 2028. In other words, Broadcom is forecasting one doubling, followed by another doubling.' \npair-old-3 e5304 'The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.' \npair-old-3 e5307 'If we think of the Data Center Interconnect or the telecom market being sort of a 1x multiple, what we are seeing now for scale-across is probably 10x of what we saw for DCI. What we are seeing now for scale-out is probably 10x of what we are seeing for DCI. What we are seeing for scale-up, starting in the second half of 2027 for the first instance of CPO [co-packaged optics] going to scale-up, is' \npair-old-3 e5316 'He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.' \npair-old-3 e5320 'Megaspeed International, a Southeast Asian importer that handled approximately $4.6 billion worth of NVIDIA hardware between 2022 and 2025.' \npair-old-3 e5322 'Additionally, roughly $13.4 million worth of this hardware was moved across 50 shipments through Southeast Asian trade routes.' \npair-old-3 e5353 'Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July.' \npair-old-3 e5356 'He said stocks later consolidated after the $65 billion figure fell short of the roughly $75 billion investors had expected.' \npair-old-3 e5361 'That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.' \npair-old-3 e5390 'Amazon AWS and Annapurna Labs are also collaborating with us to integrate custom IP into the base die of NVHBM, unlocking 30% to 40% of computing resources on their custom chips while leveraging NVIDIA SerDes to achieve higher bandwidth and lower latency.' \nsingle-O e2080 'Bank of America estimates that NVIDIA has committed approximately $300 billion in capital to its ecosystem partners, comprising about $70 billion in equity investments and roughly $230 billion in residual value guarantees or backstop commitments.' \nsingle-O e2687 'The firm estimates roughly $300 billion of committed capital to date, including about $70 billion of direct equity investments and $230 billion of guarantees or backstops.' \nsingle-O e3934 'Nvidia is separately in discussions to invest approximately $2.5 billion' \nsingle-O e4648 'Nvidia could invest as much as $10 billion' \nsingle-O e4956 'Out of the roughly 20 neoclouds GDT is working with, about 25 percent of them have received backing from Nvidia in the form of equity investments, according to Kapusta.' \nsingle-S e2489 'U.S. hyperscalers are expected to spend roughly $916 billion on capital expenditures over the next 12 months, with consensus estimates projecting that figure to rise to nearly $1.2 trillion the year after.' \nsingle-E e5402 'Here, the 5th Gen EPYC CPUs with 192 cores provide a 37% gain over NVIDIA Vera & the 6th Gen EPYC Venice CPU with 256 cores provides a 2.37x gain.' \nsingle-E e5404 \"AMD's EPYC Venice delivered 18% faster memory bandwidth versus NVIDIA's Vera thanks to its 16-channel memory design, which supports up to 12,800 MT/s RDIMM modules. This provides the platform with 1.6 TB/s of memory bandwidth versus 1.2 TB/s bandwidth on the NVIDIA Vera CPUs (using LPDDR5x).\" \npassages 815\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
