{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'readers|A4|forecast of|same base|source|sum' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r53.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:**Not ready.** The revised rules can reject a correct sum of two Data Center quarters and accept a Data Center forecast that is larger than company revenue at every possible value. Both are within D737’s scope. A4 should be the decisive $0 check once the written rules and their test cases agree.\n5:1. **High · (a), (c), (d) · S8 confuses what a number is with what was used to calculate it.** In P, the shown figures support calculating Q3 Data Center revenue as `share($108B, 92.5%) = $99.9B`. If Q4 is calculated the same way, adding the two Data Center quarters is valid. Yet each operand **is** Data Center revenue and **uses** company revenue, so the written rule rejects the sum. It also rejects adding a segment back to the remainder calculated as `company − segment`, even though that reconstructs the company total. Conversely, the separate P-v4 request loses the relation entirely because `only()` clears it. A company answer can then add Data Center revenue into total revenue without S8 firing on that first reply. The rule needs to distinguish an operand that adds an already-counted part from one that merely uses the whole to calculate a share or remainder. [SMALL-DESIGN.md:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:45) · [paid_gate.py:63](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:63)\n13:5. **High · (e) · The blind test still has conflicting pass conditions and reader inputs.** A1 still requires `$4.5 billion ± 3%` as two sources, while S1 requires the complete expression as one source. A2 says each entry is refused, then adds an estimate that must be accepted and recorded. The final A3 stop line still allows a mistake that is merely “stated.” And §5 tells readers to mark broken structure without clearly stopping on an accepted reply with broken structure. The existing card builder gives each reader only named passages and splits the joint calculation into per-member cards. That view can hide the two paths needed to spot a duplicate forecast. Part B needs the whole first reply and all shown passages, including for refused replies, before the checker’s decision is revealed. [SMALL-DESIGN.md:175](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:175) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:215](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:215) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:244](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:267](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:267) · [paid_gate.py:457](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:457)\n15:6. **Medium · (a), (c), (d) · The arithmetic and source instructions still leave different implementations possible.** For `ratio(F1,F1)` with a nonzero range `[100,120]`, the result is exactly `1x` because both operands are the same figure. Treating the two occurrences as independent gives `[5/6,6/5]`. “Compute both extremes” leaves that distinction unstated. The `operation` description also omits §2’s zero-containing denominator refusal and leaves “when its inputs are periods of one quantity” without an explicit sum/difference limit. Read literally across operations, it can reject a correct year-over-year growth calculation. For sources, S includes an actual `$195 billion to $205 billion` range (`e1254`), and P shows `(+/-2%)` (`e4963`). The grammar needs to say which spellings count as the complete expression so a writer and checker agree where it starts and ends. [SMALL-DESIGN.md:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:42) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:86) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:88) · [calc_check.py:125](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:125)\n21:| **S8 indirect addition** | “A sum never adds a figure that uses (or is) the part's quantity to one that uses (or is) the whole's.” This catches the `× 1x` example when the relation is present. The false refusals and separate-arm gap remain. “An estimate that rests on both the part and the whole is recorded for readers” correctly leaves the estimate’s judgement to readers. [Design:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:45) |\n23:| **S5 reference root** | **Closed.** “The figure marked in `reference_for` and every figure beneath it (inputs and rests_on) is a source, or computed with no basis forecast.” The quoted outside figure “may be the marked figure itself.” That rejects an own estimate at the root and accepts a direct outside quote. [Design:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:47) |\n26:| **S1 compound quotes** | “`$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%` is copied whole, and gives its range as low and high or its midpoint as value.” This closes the original one-sided reading for that spelling. `US$`, `bn`, `twice`, `near` and non-US currency now have stated treatment. The old two-source fixture and the actual archive spellings above remain open. [Design:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:42) · [Design:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:86) |\n27:| **S8 remainder and period spelling** | “A difference may subtract the part from the whole only to give the rest, another scope.” This allows the direct remainder. “‘first half’ is refused by S8 when summed” settles the observed alias. The text still needs to state the same-period requirement for that remainder, and which canonical half-year labels pass so P can correctly express `FY − H1 = H2`. [Design:45](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:45) · [Design:238](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:238) |\n28:| **Outcome, unresolved answers and IDs** | **Closed for the original cases.** “It is a computed or estimate figure with basis forecast” excludes a source as the outcome, while allowing an own forecast to agree with consensus. “Unresolved: why; rung and reference_unavailable null; no figure marked for it” removes the contradiction with the required answer fields. “Ids are unique and never equal a passage id” resolves the collision. The separate cycle issue remains. [Design:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:48) · [Design:89](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:89) |\n30:| **Format selection through reconciliation and cards** | **Closed as an A4 requirement, unverified.** “One v13s reply goes through the first attempt, the separate-arm reconciliation, the card render and recovery.” The existing reconciliation and card paths still invoke the legacy decoder and checker. Include the diagnostic card path, which reads the same wire format. [Design:240](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:240) · [paid_gate.py:266](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:266) · [paid_gate.py:501](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:501) · [paid_gate.py:581](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:581) |\n35:Resolve those contracts before implementation, then run A4 with each counterexample paired with its correct counterpart through the actual request, checker, reconciliation where relevant, and reader output. I checked the stored case inputs and the arithmetic examples read-only. A4 was not run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py | sed -n '315,520p'\"","aggregated_output":"   315\t# ---------- A2: defects are refused by their named rule ----------\n   316\tdef defect(name, rule, mutate, family=PAIR, base=base_pair, recorded=None):\n   317\t    @case('A2', name, rule, recorded)\n   318\t    def _():\n   319\t        a = base()\n   320\t        mutate(a)\n   321\t        return a, family\n   322\t\n   323\t\n   324\tdefect('108.5 for \"$108.0 billion\" (S1)', 'S1', lambda a: fig(a, 'F3').update(value=108.5))\n   325\tdefect('a qualifier the quote does not write (S1)', 'S1', lambda a: fig(a, 'F1').update(qualifier='about'))\n   326\tdefect('a number not written in the quote (S1)', 'S1', lambda a: fig(a, 'F1').update(quote_number='$81.62 billion', value=81.62))\n   327\tdefect('\"± 2%\" read as a positive point 110.16 (S1)', 'S1', lambda a: fig(a, 'F3').update(value=110.16))\n   328\tdefect('a plain wrong sum (S2)', 'S2', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(value=410.0))\n   329\tdefect('money × % through product (S2)', 'S2', lambda a: fig(a, 'F10').update(operation='product'))\n   330\tdefect('a three-input difference (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(operation='difference'))\n   331\tdefect('a part forecast above the whole for Q3 (S3)', 'S3', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F9').update(value=92.5), fig(a, 'F10').update(\n   332\t    kind='estimate', basis_text='segment', inputs=None, operation=None, value=112.0, rests_on=['F4']), fig(a, 'F12').update(value=382.675)))\n   333\tdefect('a part outcome above the whole outcome (S3)', 'S3', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F12').update(\n   334\t    kind='estimate', basis_text='segment', inputs=None, operation=None, value=405.0, rests_on=['F10']), a['answers'][1].update(rung=1)))\n   335\tdefect('Data Center added into company in one sum (S8)', 'S8', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   336\t    'BAD', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=775.225, inputs=['F6', 'F12'], operation='sum')))\n   337\tdefect('Q2 + Q3 labelled H1 (S8)', 'S8', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   338\t    'BAD', W('company', 'FY2027 H1'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=206.2, inputs=['F2', 'F4'], operation='sum')))\n   339\tdefect('FY − Q1 labelled Q4 (S8)', 'S8', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   340\t    'BAD', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'computed', 'consensus', 'USD bn', value=329.4, inputs=['F13', 'F1'], operation='difference')))\n   341\tdefect('two forecasts of one shared quarter (S4)', 'S4', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   342\t    'BAD', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=112.0, basis_text='another view')))\n   343\tdefect('Q3 guidance used directly beside the Q3 forecast (S4)', 'S4', lambda a: fig(a, 'F10').update(inputs=['F3', 'F9'], value=99.9))\n   344\tdefect('two Data Center Q4 forecasts (S4)', 'S4', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   345\t    'BAD', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=104.0, basis_text='another view')))\n   346\tdefect('an estimate marked as the reference (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: (a['figures'].append(F(\n   347\t    'R8', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=380.0, basis_text='looks like consensus', rests_on=['F13'],\n   348\t    reference_for=['v8'])), a['answers'][1].update(reference_unavailable=None)))\n   349\tdefect('a computed reference with basis forecast (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: (a['figures'].append(F(\n   350\t    'R8', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=380.175, inputs=['F13', 'F9'], operation='share',\n   351\t    reference_for=['v8'])), a['answers'][1].update(reference_unavailable=None)))\n   352\tdefect('a reference resting on an estimate (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: (a['figures'].append(F(\n   353\t    'R8', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'consensus', 'USD bn', value=373.45, inputs=['F13', 'M'], operation='share',\n   354\t    reference_for=['v8'])), a['figures'].append(F('M', W('Data Center', 'FY2027', measure='mix'), 'estimate', 'forecast', '%', value=90.86,\n   355\t                                                    basis_text='mix')), a['answers'][1].update(reference_unavailable=None)))\n   356\tdefect('a reported-only reference (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F1').update(reference_for=['v8']), a['answers'][1].update(reference_unavailable=None)))\n   357\tdefect('both a reference figure and a reason (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: a['answers'][0].update(reference_unavailable='also none'))\n   358\tdefect('neither a reference figure nor a reason (S5)', 'S5', lambda a: a['answers'][1].update(reference_unavailable=None))\n   359\tdefect('no outcome marker (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: fig(a, 'F12').update(outcome_for=[]))\n   360\tdefect('two outcome markers (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: fig(a, 'F11').update(outcome_for=['v8']))\n   361\tdefect('a marker on an unresolved member (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: a['answers'][1].update(shape='unresolved', why='none', rung=None,\n   362\t                                                                                     reference_unavailable=None))\n   363\tdefect('an outcome key mismatch (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: fig(a, 'F12').update(what=W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q4')))\n   364\tdefect('a source as the outcome (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F12').update(outcome_for=[]), a['figures'].append(F(\n   365\t    'SRC', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=300.0, evidence_id='e7', quote_number='$300 billion',\n   366\t    qualifier='over', outcome_for=['v8'])), a['answers'][1].update(rung=3)))\n   367\tdefect('a share above 100% (S2)', 'S2', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F9').update(kind='estimate', basis='forecast', evidence_id=None, quote_number=None,\n   368\t    qualifier=None, value=110.0, basis_text='mix'), fig(a, 'F10').update(value=121.0), fig(a, 'F11').update(value=126.5),\n   369\t    fig(a, 'F12').update(value=411.8)))\n   370\tdefect('a rung outside the ladder (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: a['answers'][0].update(rung=9))\n   371\tdefect('a rung whose band misses the outcome (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: a['answers'][0].update(rung=1))\n   372\tdefect('a declared value within tolerance whose recomputed value crosses the edge (S6)', 'S6', lambda a: (\n   373\t    fig(a, 'F5').update(value=104.3), fig(a, 'F6').update(value=391.9), a['answers'][0].update(rung=3),\n   374\t    fig(a, 'F11').update(value=96.4775), fig(a, 'F12').update(value=362.5275)))\n   375\tdefect('value with low (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F1').update(low=80.0))\n   376\tdefect('a cycle through rests_on (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F4').update(rests_on=['F5']))\n   377\tdefect('a passage id in inputs (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(inputs=['F1', 'e2', 'F4', 'F5']))\n   378\tdefect('a source with basis forecast (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F3').update(basis='forecast'))\n   379\tdefect('duplicate member answers (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: a['answers'].append(A('v4', rung=2, reference_unavailable='x')))\n   380\tdefect('a figure id equal to a passage id (S7)', 'S7', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   381\t    'e1', W('company', 'FY2027 Q1'), 'estimate', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=81.6, basis_text='copy')))\n   382\tdefect('an estimate resting on both part and whole (recorded, not refused)', 'pass', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   383\t    'BOTH', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='combined'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=775.0, basis_text='both', rests_on=['F6', 'F12'])),\n   384\t    recorded='part and whole in one estimate')\n   385\tdefect('Data Center × 1x added to company (recorded as a conversion, not refused: D738)', 'pass', lambda a: a['figures'] + [\n   386\t    a['figures'].append(F('ONE', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='factor'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', value=1.0, basis_text='one')),\n   387\t    a['figures'].append(F('ADJ', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='revenue adjustment'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=372.425,\n   388\t                          inputs=['F12', 'ONE'], operation='product'))], recorded='conversion between quantities')\n   389\t\n   390\t\n   391\t@case('A2', 'division by a range that contains zero (S2)', 'S2')\n   392\tdef _():\n   393\t    figs = [F('Z', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='z'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', low=-1.0, high=1.0, basis_text='z'),\n   394\t            F('N', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='n'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=10.0, basis_text='n'),\n   395\t            F('O', W('a', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=0.0, inputs=['N', 'Z'], operation='ratio', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   396\t    return one(figs)                                     # 0.0 is the midpoint of the vertices: only the zero-divisor rule refuses it\n   397\t\n   398\t\n   399\t@case('A2', '[-3, -2] × [2, 4] declared other than [-12, -4] (S2)', 'S2')\n   400\tdef _():\n   401\t    figs = [F('P', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='p'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', low=-3.0, high=-2.0, basis_text='p'),\n   402\t            F('Q', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='q'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', low=2.0, high=4.0, basis_text='q'),\n   403\t            F('R', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='r'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'x', low=-8.0, high=-6.0, inputs=['P', 'Q'], operation='product'),\n   404\t            F('O', W('a', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=1.0, basis_text='o', rests_on=['R'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   405\t    return one(figs)\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t@case('A2', 'a figure used twice takes one value: ratio(F, F) over a range is 1, not a spread (passes)', 'pass')\n   409\tdef _():\n   410\t    figs = [F('P', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='p'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', low=50.0, high=150.0, basis_text='p'),\n   411\t            F('R', W('a', 'FY2027', measure='r'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'x', value=1.0, inputs=['P', 'P'], operation='ratio'),\n   412\t            F('O', W('a', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=1.0, basis_text='o', rests_on=['R'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   413\t    return one(figs)\n   414\t\n   415\t\n   416\t@case('A2', 'a euro amount as a source (S1)', 'S1')\n   417\tdef _():\n   418\t    figs = [F('S', W('program', 'FY2027', measure='cost'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=5.0, evidence_id='e15', quote_number='€5 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   419\t            F('O', W('program', 'FY2027', measure='cost'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=5.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   420\t    return one(figs)\n   421\t\n   422\t\n   423\t@case('A2', 'trillions written as 1.2 USD bn (S1)', 'S1')\n   424\tdef _():\n   425\t    figs = [F('S', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=1.2, evidence_id='e13', quote_number='$1.2 trillion', qualifier='none'),\n   426\t            F('O', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=1.25, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   427\t    return one(figs)\n   428\t\n   429\t\n   430\t@case('A2', '\"-3%\" taken as 3 (S1)', 'S1')\n   431\tdef _():\n   432\t    figs = [F('S', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='margin change'), 'source', 'reported', '%', value=3.0, evidence_id='e12', quote_number='3%', qualifier='none'),\n   433\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=10.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   434\t    return one(figs)\n   435\t\n   436\t\n   437\t@case('A2', 'a qualifier dropped: \"over $300 billion\" as none (S1)', 'S1')\n   438\tdef _():\n   439\t    figs = [F('S', W('Data Center', 'FY2028'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=300.0, evidence_id='e7', quote_number='$300 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   440\t            F('O', W('Data Center', 'FY2028'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=320.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   441\t    return one(figs)\n   442\t\n   443\t\n   444\t@case('A2', 'an outcome at the band\\'s upper edge (S6)', 'S6')\n   445\tdef _():\n   446\t    figs = [F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=400.0, basis_text='x', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   447\t    return one(figs, rung=2, family=single(W('company', 'FY2027'), ((400.0, None), (350.0, 400.0))))\n   448\t\n   449\t\n   450\t# ---------- A3: Luna's observed mistakes, encoded in v13s ----------\n   451\tdef luna(name, expect, mutate, base=base_pair, family=PAIR):\n   452\t    @case('A3', name, expect)\n   453\t    def _():\n   454\t        a = base()\n   455\t        mutate(a)\n   456\t        return a, family\n   457\t\n   458\t\n   459\tluna('a prose outcome (an outcome marker must name a member)', 'schema', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(outcome_for=['$398.1 billion']))\n   460\tluna('a prose evidence id', 'schema', lambda a: fig(a, 'F1').update(evidence_id='NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion.'))\n   461\tluna('a prose reference (a reference marker must name a member)', 'schema', lambda a: fig(a, 'F13').update(reference_for=['Analyst consensus of $411 billion']))\n   462\tluna('a unit spelled \"USD billions\"', 'schema', lambda a: fig(a, 'F1').update(unit='USD billions'))\n   463\tluna('value with a range (both given)', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F3').update(low=105.84, high=110.16))\n   464\tluna('a four-input difference', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(operation='difference'))\n   465\tluna('money × % through product', 'S2', lambda a: (fig(a, 'F10').update(operation='product', value=10175.0),\n   466\t                                                  fig(a, 'F12').update(value=10445.675)))      # arithmetic consistent: only the unit rule refuses it\n   467\tluna('\"FY2027 first half\" summed from quarters', 'S8', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   468\t    'H1', W('company', 'FY2027 first half'), 'computed', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=177.8, inputs=['F1', 'F2'], operation='sum')))\n   469\tluna('a passage id in inputs', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(inputs=['e1', 'F2', 'F4', 'F5']))\n   470\tluna('prose in inputs', 'S7', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(inputs=['Q1 revenue', 'F2', 'F4', 'F5']))\n   471\tluna('an outcome in \"USD trillion\"', 'schema', lambda a: fig(a, 'F6').update(unit='USD trillion'))\n   472\tluna('\"65% growth in Q4\" copied as the number', 'S1', lambda a: a['figures'].append(F(\n   473\t    'G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4', measure='growth'), 'source', 'third_party', '%', value=65.0, evidence_id='e8', quote_number='65% growth in Q4',\n   474\t    qualifier='none')))\n   475\t\n   476\t\n   477\tdef main():\n   478\t    failures = 0\n   479\t    for group, name, expect, recorded, build in CASES:\n   480\t        answer, family = build()\n   481\t        result = run(copy.deepcopy(answer), family)\n   482\t        if 'schema' in result:\n   483\t            got = 'schema'\n   484\t            detail = result['schema'][:1]\n   485\t        else:\n   486\t            codes = sorted({c for c, _ in result['errors']})\n   487\t            got = 'pass' if not codes else ','.join(codes)\n   488\t            detail = result['errors'][:2]\n   489\t        ok = (got == 'pass') if expect == 'pass' else (expect == 'schema' and got == 'schema') or (expect in got.split(','))\n   490\t        if ok and recorded:\n   491\t            ok = any(r['type'] == recorded for r in result.get('recorded', []))\n   492\t            if not ok:\n   493\t                detail = [f'missing recorded {recorded}: {[r[\"type\"] for r in result.get(\"recorded\", [])]}']\n   494\t        failures += not ok\n   495\t        print(f'{\"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\"}  {group}  {name}  [expected {expect}{\" + recorded \" + recorded if recorded else \"\"}; got {got}]'\n   496\t              + ('' if ok else f'  {json.dumps(detail, ensure_ascii=False)[:400]}'))\n   497\t    print(f'{len(CASES) - failures} of {len(CASES)} cases as registered')\n   498\t    return 1 if failures else 0\n   499\t\n   500\t\n   501\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   502\t    raise SystemExit(main())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The v13s small format's Part A cases (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [52], D738): A1 correct forms pass, A2 defects are refused by their named\n     2\trule (or recorded, where D738 says so), A3 Luna's observed mistakes are impossible under the schema or refused by their stated rule.\n     3\tEach case runs the real path: the v13s schema (model.check_schema), calc_small.from_answer, calc_small.check. $0.\n     4\tUsage: python3 small_cases.py   (prints one line per case; exit 1 on any failure).\"\"\"\n     5\timport copy\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport os\n     8\timport sys\n     9\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    10\t\n    11\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    12\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    13\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    14\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    15\tif os.environ.get('CALC_SMALL_DIR'):                     # small_mutants.py: a mutated calc_small.py on a scratch copy\n    16\t    sys.path.insert(0, os.environ['CALC_SMALL_DIR'])\n    17\timport calc_small as cs  # noqa: E402\n    18\timport render_v13 as rv  # noqa: E402\n    19\tfrom hivemind import model  # noqa: E402\n    20\t\n    21\tFIELDS = ['id', 'what', 'kind', 'basis', 'value', 'low', 'high', 'unit', 'evidence_id', 'quote_number', 'qualifier', 'inputs', 'operation',\n    22\t          'basis_text', 'rests_on', 'outcome_for', 'reference_for']\n    23\tPASSAGES = {\n    24\t    'e1': 'First-quarter revenue was $81.6 billion, up 85% from a year ago.',\n    25\t    'e2': 'Second-quarter revenue was $96.2 billion.',\n    26\t    'e3': 'Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.',\n    27\t    'e4': 'Data Center revenue was $75.3 billion in the first quarter.',\n    28\t    'e5': 'Data Center revenue was $89.0 billion in the second quarter, 92.5% of total revenue.',\n    29\t    'e6': 'Analysts expect full-year revenue of $411 billion.',\n    30\t    'e7': 'Data center revenue will be well over $300 billion next year.',\n    31\t    'e8': 'and 65% growth in Q4.',\n    32\t    'e9': 'Fourth-quarter revenue a year ago was $68.1 billion.',\n    33\t    'e10': 'the company not only still expects $20 billion in sales, but roughly twice that number next year.',\n    34\t    'e11': 'A plant costing $300 million or more is planned.',\n    35\t    'e12': 'Margins moved -3% in the period.',\n    36\t    'e13': 'Combined spending reached $1.2 trillion.',\n    37\t    'e14': 'The bonds total US$10 billion; sales were $96.2bn; the range is between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion.',\n    38\t    'e15': 'The program costs €5 billion.',\n    39\t    'e16': 'Spending will not be over $300 billion.',\n    40\t    'e17': 'Unit prices rose 12% and volumes doubled.',\n    41\t    'e18': 'Spending is tracked at $745 billion.',\n    42\t    'e19': 'Another estimate puts spending at $760 billion.',\n    43\t}\n    44\tPASSAGES = {k: {'text': v, 'speaker': 'an outlet'} for k, v in PASSAGES.items()}\n    45\tEVIDENCE = sorted(PASSAGES)\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\tdef W(scope, period, measure='revenue', population='NVIDIA'):\n    49\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tPAIR = {'members': {'v4': {'what': W('company', 'FY2027'), 'unit': 'USD bn',\n    53\t                           'bands': [[431.2, None], [392.0, 431.2], [352.8, 392.0], [313.6, 352.8], [None, 313.6]]},\n    54\t                    'v8': {'what': W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'unit': 'USD bn',\n    55\t                           'bands': [[400.0, None], [350.0, 400.0], [300.0, 350.0], [250.0, 300.0], [None, 250.0]]}},\n    56\t        'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': 'v8', 'whole': 'v4'}],\n    57\t        'shared': [W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), W('company', 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    58\t        'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027'],\n    59\t        'part_scopes': [{'population': 'NVIDIA', 'measure': 'revenue', 'part': 'Data Center', 'whole': 'company'}]}\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef F(id, what, kind, basis, unit, **kw):\n    63\t    f = {k: None for k in FIELDS}\n    64\t    f.update(id=id, what=what, kind=kind, basis=basis, unit=unit, outcome_for=[], reference_for=[])\n    65\t    f.update(kw)\n    66\t    return f\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\tdef A(view, shape='forecast', rung=None, reference_unavailable=None, why=None):\n    70\t    return {'view_id': view, 'shape': shape, 'rung': rung, 'reference_unavailable': reference_unavailable, 'reasons': 'case',\n    71\t            'why': why, 'cites': [], 'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': []}\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\tdef base_pair():\n    75\t    \"\"\"A correct joint answer: company quarters, one shared Q3/Q4 forecast, Data Center quarters through share, a consensus reference.\"\"\"\n    76\t    figs = [\n    77\t        F('F1', W('company', 'FY2027 Q1'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=81.6, evidence_id='e1', quote_number='$81.6 billion', qualifier='none'),\n    78\t        F('F2', W('company', 'FY2027 Q2'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=96.2, evidence_id='e2', quote_number='$96.2 billion', qualifier='none'),\n    79\t        F('F3', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'source', 'guidance', 'USD bn', value=108.0, evidence_id='e3',\n    80\t          quote_number='$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', qualifier='none'),\n    81\t        F('F4', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=110.0, basis_text='a small beat on guidance', rests_on=['F3']),\n    82\t        F('F5', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=115.0, basis_text='growth continues', rests_on=['F4']),\n    83\t        F('F6', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=402.8, inputs=['F1', 'F2', 'F4', 'F5'], operation='sum',\n    84\t          outcome_for=['v4']),\n    85\t        F('F7', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q1'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=75.3, evidence_id='e4', quote_number='$75.3 billion', qualifier='none'),\n    86\t        F('F8', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q2'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=89.0, evidence_id='e5', quote_number='$89.0 billion', qualifier='none'),\n    87\t        F('F9', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q2', measure='share of revenue'), 'source', 'reported', '%', value=92.5, evidence_id='e5',\n    88\t          quote_number='92.5%', qualifier='none'),\n    89\t        F('F10', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=101.75, inputs=['F4', 'F9'], operation='share'),\n    90\t        F('F11', W('Data Center', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=106.375, inputs=['F5', 'F9'], operation='share'),\n    91\t        F('F12', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=372.425, inputs=['F7', 'F8', 'F10', 'F11'], operation='sum',\n    92\t          outcome_for=['v8']),\n    93\t        F('F13', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'source', 'consensus', 'USD bn', value=411.0, evidence_id='e6', quote_number='$411 billion',\n    94\t          qualifier='none', reference_for=['v4']),\n    95\t    ]\n    96\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': [A('v4', rung=2), A('v8', rung=2, reference_unavailable='no market figure for this segment')]}\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\tdef single(what, bands=((None, None),)):\n   100\t    return {'members': {'s': {'what': what, 'unit': 'USD bn', 'bands': [list(b) for b in bands]}}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [],\n   101\t            'compare_periods': [], 'part_scopes': []}\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\tdef one(figs, rung=1, family=None, reference_unavailable='none shown'):\n   105\t    fam = family or single(figs[-1]['what'], ((None, None),))\n   106\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': [A('s', rung=rung, reference_unavailable=reference_unavailable)]}, fam\n   107\t\n   108\t\n   109\tdef run(answer, family, passages=PASSAGES):\n   110\t    members = sorted(family['members'])\n   111\t    schema = rv.v13s_schema(members, EVIDENCE, [])\n   112\t    schema_errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\n   113\t    if schema_errors:\n   114\t        return {'schema': schema_errors}\n   115\t    calc = cs.from_answer(answer, family)\n   116\t    return cs.check(family, passages, calc)\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\tdef fig(answer, fid):\n   120\t    return next(f for f in answer['figures'] if f['id'] == fid)\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\tCASES = []\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\tdef case(group, name, expect, recorded=None):\n   127\t    def wrap(build):\n   128\t        CASES.append((group, name, expect, recorded, build))\n   129\t        return build\n   130\t    return wrap\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t# ---------- A1: correct forms pass ----------\n   134\t@case('A1', 'the base joint answer', 'pass')\n   135\tdef _():\n   136\t    return base_pair(), PAIR\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t@case('A1', '$108.0B ± 2% as a range (low and high)', 'pass')\n   140\tdef _():\n   141\t    a = base_pair()\n   142\t    fig(a, 'F3').update(value=None, low=105.84, high=110.16)\n   143\t    return a, PAIR\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\t@case('A1', 'Q1 + Q2 = H1, then H1 + Q3 + Q4 = FY', 'pass')\n   147\tdef _():\n   148\t    a = base_pair()\n   149\t    a['figures'].append(F('H1', W('company', 'FY2027 H1'), 'computed', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=177.8, inputs=['F1', 'F2'], operation='sum'))\n   150\t    fig(a, 'F6').update(inputs=['H1', 'F4', 'F5'])\n   151\t    return a, PAIR\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t@case('A1', 'FY − Q1-Q3 = Q4 (a residual)', 'pass')\n   155\tdef _():\n   156\t    a = base_pair()\n   157\t    a['figures'] += [F('N9', W('company', 'FY2027 Q1-Q3'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=287.8, inputs=['F1', 'F2', 'F4'], operation='sum'),\n   158\t                     F('C4', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'computed', 'consensus', 'USD bn', value=123.2, inputs=['F13', 'N9'], operation='difference')]\n   159\t    return a, PAIR\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t@case('A1', 'a year-over-year rate on last year\\'s quarter (recorded, not refused)', 'pass', recorded='carried across periods')\n   163\tdef _():\n   164\t    figs = [F('B', W('company', 'FY2026 Q4'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=68.1, evidence_id='e9', quote_number='$68.1 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   165\t            F('G', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4', measure='revenue growth'), 'source', 'third_party', '%', value=65.0, evidence_id='e8', quote_number='65%', qualifier='none'),\n   166\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2027 Q4'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=112.365, inputs=['B', 'G'], operation='apply_growth', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   167\t    return one(figs)\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t@case('A1', 'a whole times a mix through share', 'pass')\n   171\tdef _():\n   172\t    a = base_pair()\n   173\t    return a, PAIR\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t@case('A1', '\"over $300 billion\" (from \"well over $300 billion\") with qualifier over', 'pass', recorded='qualified source')\n   177\tdef _():\n   178\t    figs = [F('S', W('Data Center', 'FY2028'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=300.0, evidence_id='e7', quote_number='$300 billion', qualifier='over'),\n   179\t            F('O', W('Data Center', 'FY2028'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=320.0, basis_text='above the outside figure', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   180\t    return one(figs)\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t@case('A1', '\"-3%\" as written', 'pass')\n   184\tdef _():\n   185\t    figs = [F('S', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='margin change'), 'source', 'reported', '%', value=-3.0, evidence_id='e12', quote_number='-3%', qualifier='none'),\n   186\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=10.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   187\t    return one(figs)\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t@case('A1', '\"$300 million or more\" with qualifier \"or more\"', 'pass')\n   191\tdef _():\n   192\t    figs = [F('S', W('plant', 'FY2027', measure='cost'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=0.3, evidence_id='e11', quote_number='$300 million', qualifier='or more'),\n   193\t            F('O', W('plant', 'FY2027', measure='cost'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=0.35, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   194\t    return one(figs)\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\t@case('A1', '$1.2 trillion as 1200 USD bn', 'pass')\n   198\tdef _():\n   199\t    figs = [F('S', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=1200.0, evidence_id='e13', quote_number='$1.2 trillion', qualifier='none'),\n   200\t            F('O', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=1250.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['S'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   201\t    return one(figs, family=single(W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), ((1000.0, 1500.0),)))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t@case('A1', 'a range outcome overlapping its rung', 'pass')\n   205\tdef _():\n   206\t    figs = [F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', low=380.0, high=400.0, basis_text='a range', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   207\t    return one(figs, rung=2, family=single(W('company', 'FY2027'), ((400.0, None), (350.0, 400.0))))\n   208\t\n   209\t\n   210\t@case('A1', 'one figure marked for two members', 'pass')\n   211\tdef _():\n   212\t    fam = {'members': {'a': {'what': W('company', 'FY2027'), 'unit': 'USD bn', 'bands': [[None, None]]},\n   213\t                       'b': {'what': W('company', 'FY2027'), 'unit': 'USD bn', 'bands': [[None, None]]}},\n   214\t           'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': [], 'part_scopes': []}\n   215\t    figs = [F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=400.0, basis_text='x', outcome_for=['a', 'b'])]\n   216\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': [A('a', rung=1, reference_unavailable='none'), A('b', rung=1, reference_unavailable='none')]}, fam\n   217\t\n   218\t\n   219\t@case('A1', 'a computed external reference (consensus × reported mix)', 'pass')\n   220\tdef _():\n   221\t    a = base_pair()\n   222\t    a['figures'].append(F('R8', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'consensus', 'USD bn', value=380.175, inputs=['F13', 'F9'], operation='share',\n   223\t                          reference_for=['v8']))\n   224\t    a['answers'][1]['reference_unavailable'] = None\n   225\t    return a, PAIR\n   226\t\n   227\t\n   228\t@case('A1', 'an unresolved member', 'pass')\n   229\tdef _():\n   230\t    a = base_pair()\n   231\t    a['figures'] = [f for f in a['figures'] if f['id'] not in ('F7', 'F8', 'F10', 'F11', 'F12')]\n   232\t    a['answers'][1] = A('v8', shape='unresolved', why='no segment figure is shown')\n   233\t    return a, PAIR\n   234\t\n   235\t\n   236\t@case('A1', 'a conversion between quantities (recorded, not refused)', 'pass', recorded='conversion between quantities')\n   237\tdef _():\n   238\t    figs = [F('S1', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=745.0, evidence_id='e18',\n   239\t              quote_number='$745 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   240\t            F('M', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='data-center share'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', value=0.8, basis_text='most capex is data centers'),\n   241\t            F('O', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='data-center capex'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=596.0, inputs=['S1', 'M'],\n   242\t              operation='product', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   243\t    return one(figs)\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t@case('A1', '\"not only still expects $20 billion\" as a source, \"roughly twice\" as a multiple', 'pass')\n   247\tdef _():\n   248\t    figs = [F('B', W('company', 'FY2027', measure='CPU sales'), 'source', 'guidance', 'USD bn', value=20.0, evidence_id='e10', quote_number='$20 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   249\t            F('X', W('company', 'FY2028', measure='CPU sales multiple'), 'source', 'guidance', 'x', value=2.0, evidence_id='e10', quote_number='twice', qualifier='roughly'),\n   250\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2028', measure='CPU sales'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=40.0, inputs=['B', 'X'], operation='product', outcome_for=['s'])]\n   251\t    return one(figs)\n   252\t\n   253\t\n   254\t@case('A1', '12% × 2x = 24%', 'pass')\n   255\tdef _():\n   256\t    figs = [F('P', W('unit', 'FY2027', measure='price change'), 'source', 'reported', '%', value=12.0, evidence_id='e17', quote_number='12%', qualifier='none'),\n   257\t            F('X', W('unit', 'FY2027', measure='factor'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', value=2.0, basis_text='two steps'),\n   258\t            F('Q', W('unit', 'FY2027', measure='price change'), 'computed', 'forecast', '%', value=24.0, inputs=['P', 'X'], operation='product'),\n   259\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=10.0, basis_text='x', rests_on=['Q'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   260\t    return one(figs)\n   261\t\n   262\t\n   263\t@case('A1', 'US$10 billion, $96.2bn, a written range', 'pass')\n   264\tdef _():\n   265\t    figs = [F('A1', W('bonds', 'FY2027', measure='size'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=10.0, evidence_id='e14', quote_number='US$10 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   266\t            F('A2', W('company', 'FY2027 Q2'), 'source', 'reported', 'USD bn', value=96.2, evidence_id='e14', quote_number='$96.2bn', qualifier='none'),\n   267\t            F('A3', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'source', 'guidance', 'USD bn', low=105.84, high=110.16, evidence_id='e14',\n   268\t              quote_number='between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   269\t            F('O', W('company', 'FY2027 Q3'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=108.0, inputs=['A3', 'A3'], operation='sum'),\n   270\t            ]\n   271\t    figs[-1].update(inputs=['A3'], operation='sum')\n   272\t    figs[-1].update(kind='estimate', inputs=None, operation=None, basis_text='the midpoint', rests_on=['A3'], outcome_for=['s'])\n   273\t    return one(figs)\n   274\t\n   275\t\n   276\t@case('A1', 'a point Data Center forecast beside a company range (lowest against highest)', 'pass')\n   277\tdef _():\n   278\t    a = base_pair()\n   279\t    fig(a, 'F4').update(value=None, low=105.84, high=110.16)\n   280\t    fig(a, 'F10').update(kind='estimate', basis_text='segment stays near its mix', inputs=None, operation=None, value=100.0, rests_on=['F4'])\n   281\t    fig(a, 'F6').update(value=None, low=398.64, high=402.96)\n   282\t    fig(a, 'F12').update(value=370.675)\n   283\t    return a, PAIR\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t@case('A1', 'a final range estimate resting on a computed point of the same quantity', 'pass', recorded='one quantity, several figures')\n   287\tdef _():\n   288\t    a = base_pair()\n   289\t    fig(a, 'F12').update(outcome_for=[], basis='forecast')\n   290\t    fig(a, 'F12').update(basis='reported')\n   291\t    a['figures'].append(F('R', W('Data Center', 'FY2027'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', low=360.0, high=385.0, basis_text='a range around it',\n   292\t                          rests_on=['F12'], outcome_for=['v8']))\n   293\t    return a, PAIR\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t@case('A1', 'two outside estimates averaged into one starting point', 'pass')\n   297\tdef _():\n   298\t    figs = [F('S1', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=745.0, evidence_id='e18', quote_number='$745 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   299\t            F('S2', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'source', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=760.0, evidence_id='e19', quote_number='$760 billion', qualifier='none'),\n   300\t            F('T', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex, two sources'), 'computed', 'third_party', 'USD bn', value=1505.0, inputs=['S1', 'S2'], operation='sum'),\n   301\t            F('H', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=752.5, inputs=['T', 'D'], operation='ratio'),\n   302\t            F('D', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='divisor'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'x', value=2.0, basis_text='two sources'),\n   303\t            F('O', W('four companies', 'CY2026', measure='capex'), 'estimate', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=752.5, basis_text='the average', rests_on=['H'], outcome_for=['s'])]\n   304\t    figs[3]['basis'] = 'third_party'\n   305\t    return one(figs)\n   306\t\n   307\t\n   308\t@case('A1', 'the remainder: company − Data Center = the rest', 'pass')\n   309\tdef _():\n   310\t    a = base_pair()\n   311\t    a['figures'].append(F('REST', W('other', 'FY2027'), 'computed', 'forecast', 'USD bn', value=30.375, inputs=['F6', 'F12'], operation='difference'))\n   312\t    return a, PAIR\n   313\t\n   314\t\n   315\t# ---------- A2: defects are refused by their named rule ----------\n   316\tdef defect(name, rule, mutate, family=PAIR, base=base_pair, recorded=None):\n   317\t    @case('A2', name, rule, recorded)\n   318\t    def _():\n   319\t        a = base()\n   320\t        mutate(a)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
