nues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e327, e1691, e1931; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e111 'First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.' 'First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e273, e274, e326, e478, e1401, e1425; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e1510 'The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027,' 'The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\npair-old-1 e2295 'Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2649 'NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.' 'NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2667, e4536; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2650 'Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago' 'Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2668; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2652 'Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.' 'Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2670, e2748, e2818, e3009, e3782; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2681 'NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.' 'NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1639, e2715, e3045, e4450; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2686 \"AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\" \"AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2664, e2787, e2878, e2879, e3056; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2691 'Customers forecasts point to our growth, doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply constrained.' 'Customers forecasts point to our growth, doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply constrained.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2846, e2950, e2973, e3114, e3210, e3326, e5202; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2693 'We commenced production shipments of Vera Rubin earlier this month, having already received purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM' 'We commenced production shipments of Vera Rubin earlier this month, having already received purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2880, e2881, e2955, e3431; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e738 (2026-07-18); both are in force: The author said NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform was slated to enter production in the second half of 2026.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2720 'Total revenue is expected to be $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.' 'Total revenue is expected to be $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2721 'We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.' 'We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2882, e3264, e3706, e4343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2723 'Data Center revenue for the second quarter was a record $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago and up 18% sequentially, driven by the ramp of our Blackwell Ultra infrastructure.' 'Data Center revenue for the second quarter was a record $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago and up 18% sequentially, driven by the ramp of our Blackwell Ultra infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2668, e2756, e2819, e2842, e3041, e3181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\npair-old-1 e2759 'We have significantly increased our supply and capacity commitments from $119 billion last quarter to $279 billion as of July 26, 2026 to meet future demand.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2759 'We have significantly increased our supply and capacity commitments from $119 billion last quarter to $279 billion as of July 26, 2026 to meet future demand.' 'We have significantly increased our supply and capacity commitments from $119 billion last quarter to $279 billion as of July 26, 2026 to meet future demand.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2730, e4109; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2776 'As of the end of the second quarter of fiscal year 2027, while we were able to ship uncontrolled products to China, such as gaming and workstation GPUs, we were effectively foreclosed from competing in China’s data center computing/compute market, and our effective foreclosure from the China market helped our competitors build larger developer and customer ecosystems to challenge us worldwide.' 'As of the end of the second quarter of fiscal year 2027, while we were able to ship uncontrolled products to China, such as gaming and workstation GPUs, we were effectively foreclosed from competing in China’s data center computing/compute market, and our effective foreclosure from the China market helped our competitors build larger developer and customer ecosystems to challenge us worldwide.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e753, e4601; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2870 \"Huang said actual demand for Nvidia's chips is far greater than 70%, but limited memory, power, and data center capacity are holding growth to that pace for now.\" \"Huang said actual demand for Nvidia's chips is far greater than 70%, but limited memory, power, and data center capacity are holding growth to that pace for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2855, e3115, e3733; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2882 'Kress said NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin to be its fastest product ramp to date and expects the platform to account for about 20% of data center revenue in the third quarter.' 'Kress said NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin to be its fastest product ramp to date and expects the platform to account for about 20% of data center revenue in the third quarter.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2721, e3213, e3405, e3589; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e2941 'Its Q3 outlook calls for revenue of $108 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 89%.' 'Its Q3 outlook calls for revenue of $108 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 89%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3077, e3125, e4523; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e3115 \"severe supply chain bottlenecks—ranging from memory availability to data center power and construction—are capping the company's near-term output.\" \"severe supply chain bottlenecks—ranging from memory availability to data center power and construction—are capping the company's near-term output.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2870; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\npair-old-1 e3200 'NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) had also excluded China Data Center compute revenue from its $91.0 billion second-quarter outlook, yet actual revenue exceeded that midpoint by $5.2 billion.'\npair-old-1 e3346 'For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e3346 'For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.' 'For the third quarter, Nvidia expects revenue between $105.84 billion and $110.16 billion, representing year-over-year growth of 85.7% to 93.2% from the $57.01 billion reported in the same quarter last year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e2941 (2026-08-26); both are in force: NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q3 revenue to $108 billion, up 89% year over year.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e3399 \"A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\" \"A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3707; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e3733 'at this moment, we have supply for 70%. We have more supply than 70%, but about 70%. Our demand is much higher than that.' 'at this moment, we have supply for 70%. We have more supply than 70%, but about 70%. Our demand is much higher than that.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2870; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4001 'For Nvidia, building up its open source business may help it cushion a demand slowdown from customers such as \\u2060Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft, which are developing their own AI chips to cut reliance \\u200bon its costly and \\u200bsupply-constrained processors.' 'For Nvidia, building up its open source business may help it cushion a demand slowdown from customers such as \\u2060Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft, which are developing their own AI chips to cut reliance \\u200bon its costly and \\u200bsupply-constrained processors.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4038; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4202 'Nvidia used to collect about $18 billion in revenue for every gigawatt of computing capacity it helped install with Hopper. With Blackwell, that figure rose to $25 billion. Kress says that with Vera Rubin, the company can reach $40 billion per gigawatt.' 'Nvidia used to collect about $18 billion in revenue for every gigawatt of computing capacity it helped install with Hopper. With Blackwell, that figure rose to $25 billion. Kress says that with Vera Rubin, the company can reach $40 billion per gigawatt.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2887; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4248 'However, this time, the company has much better visibility into memory and manufacturing capacity, as well as the land, power, and data-center infrastructure needed to deploy its products.' 'However, this time, the company has much better visibility into memory and manufacturing capacity, as well as the land, power, and data-center infrastructure needed to deploy its products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e4220 (); both are in force: NVIDIA warned that shortages of land, power, and other data-center infrastructure could delay customer hardware deployments.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4273 'In fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, the growth rate moderated to 65%, while revenue reached $215.9 billion.' 'In fiscal 2026, which ended in January 2026, the growth rate moderated to 65%, while revenue reached $215.9 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e711, e5326; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4278 'Approximately 92% of Nvidia’s revenue comes from data center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.' 'Approximately 92% of Nvidia’s revenue comes from data center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3797; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4283 'According to Nvidia’s forecast, most of the growth in the third quarter is expected to come from ACIE, while growth in hyperscale is expected to accelerate again in the fourth quarter and throughout fiscal 2028 as the supply of the Vera Rubin platform expands.' 'According to Nvidia’s forecast, most of the growth in the third quarter is expected to come from ACIE, while growth in hyperscale is expected to accelerate again in the fourth quarter and throughout fiscal 2028 as the supply of the Vera Rubin platform expands.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5061; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4333 'For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.' 'For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4294, e4375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4519 'ACIE, the sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise side of the data center business, grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.' 'ACIE, the sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise side of the data center business, grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2875; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4574 \"Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ: AMZN ) and NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) announced an expanded deal on August 26 that will bring an additional 2 million Nvidia GPU processors to Amazon data centers, building on AWS's earlier plan to add more than 1 million NVIDIA GPUs starting in 2026. The new processors, which include NVIDIA's Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs, are expected to arrive in \" \"Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ: AMZN ) and NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ: NVDA ) announced an expanded deal on August 26 that will bring an additional 2 million Nvidia GPU processors to Amazon data centers, building on AWS's earlier plan to add more than 1 million NVIDIA GPUs starting in 2026. The new processors, which include NVIDIA's Blackwell Ultra, Rubin and Rubin Ultra GPUs, are expected to arrive in \\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3410; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4575 'NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) gains a massive buyer as the company targets more than $1 trillion in Blackwell and Rubin revenue through 2027' 'NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) gains a massive buyer as the company targets more than $1 trillion in Blackwell and Rubin revenue through 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1496; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4628 \"Nvidia's management sees revenue rising to $108 billion in the third quarter, and expects full-year revenue to soar 70% over last year, which is much higher than the 44% growth consensus projection from analysts.\" \"Nvidia's management sees revenue rising to $108 billion in the third quarter, and expects full-year revenue to soar 70% over last year, which is much higher than the 44% growth consensus projection from analysts.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4046, e4703; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\nMISMATCH pair-old-1 e4772 'He pointed to Australia as an example, where Nvidia is working with companies and data-center operators on plans involving 2 gigawatts of capacity for 2027, valued at about $80 billion.' 'He pointed to Australia as an example, where Nvidia is working with companies and data-center operators on plans involving 2 gigawatts of capacity for 2027, valued at about $80 billion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the