ring, serving as an early backer that could signal strong institutional confidence to public markets preparing to absorb the astronomical valuations and capital demands of frontier artificial intelligence labs.' 'According to a Reuters exclusive , the chipmaker is weighing a US$10 billion commitment to the offering, serving as an early backer that could signal strong institutional confidence to public markets preparing to absorb the astronomical valuations and capital demands of frontier artificial intelligence labs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4648; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nsingle-O e4729 'Nvidia spent more than $42 billion buying equity stakes in other companies in the first half of the fiscal year, up from about $1.2 billion a year earlier.'\nMISMATCH single-O e4829 'NVIDIA has put nearly $50 billion into the Frontier AI labs' 'NVIDIA has put nearly $50 billion into the Frontier AI labs\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2740; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH single-S e1786 'Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will spend more than $730 billion combined on AI infrastructure this year, and they expect that number to increase next year.' 'Amazon , Meta Platforms , Microsoft , and Alphabet have indicated they will spend more than $730 billion combined on AI infrastructure this year, and they expect that number to increase next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1583, e1925; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nsingle-S e1926 'What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.'\nMISMATCH single-S e1926 'What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.' 'What analysts expect the hyperscalers to spend in 2027 alone has more than doubled in the space of a year, from a consensus of $480 billion (€416bn) in August 2025 to $1.08 trillion (€943bn) this month, a rise of about 127%, according to Bank of America.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1559, e2008; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH single-S e2535 'With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.' 'With cloud industry backlog now greater than $2 trillion, CapEx by the top 5 hyperscalers is expected to reach nearly $800 billion in 2026 and $1.3 trillion in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e465, e3124, e3306, e3307, e3372, e3401, e3405, e3485, e4112; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH single-S e4485 'On August 10, Nvidia expanded its role further by partnering with six financial institutions—Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs, and KKR—on platforms aimed at mobilizing more than $500 billion of third-party capital for AI infrastructure.' 'On August 10, Nvidia expanded its role further by partnering with six financial institutions—Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs, and KKR—on platforms aimed at mobilizing more than $500 billion of third-party capital for AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1671; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.'\nMISMATCH single-S e4739 'before pushing that figure to $1.08 trillion in 2027.' 'before pushing that figure to $1.08 trillion in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matche