{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,re\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'','\\\\''src'\\\\'']\nimport paid_gate as p\nP=p.build_plan('\\\\''v13s'\\\\'')\nfor i in P:\n if i['\\\\''arm'\\\\''].startswith('\\\\''separate'\\\\''):continue\n for e,row in i['\\\\''passages'\\\\''].items():\n  t=row['\\\\''text'\\\\'']\n  if (e in ['\\\\''e4963'\\\\'','\\\\''e1254'\\\\'','\\\\''e4867'\\\\'','\\\\''e2754'\\\\'','\\\\''e4648'\\\\'','\\\\''e4704'\\\\'','\\\\''e2497'\\\\'','\\\\''e4761'\\\\'','\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''e3660'\\\\'','\\\\''e2489'\\\\'']) or re.search(r'\\\\''between\\\\s+[-−]?\\\\d+(?:\\\\.\\\\d+)?%\\\\s+and\\\\s+[-−]?\\\\d|\\\\(\\\\s*\\\\+/-|\\\\\"'$'\"\\\\s+\\\\d|\\\\bno more than\\\\s+\\\\\"'$'\"'\\\\'',t,re.I):\n   print(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],e,repr(t))\nfor draw,calls,keys in [('\\\\''old-1'\\\\'',[('\\\\''v4'\\\\'',8810),('\\\\''v8'\\\\'',8816)],None),('\\\\''old-3'\\\\'',[('\\\\''v6'\\\\'',9043)],'\\\\''S'\\\\''),('\\\\''old-2'\\\\'',[('\\\\''v29'\\\\'',8507)],'\\\\''O'\\\\''),('\\\\''old-3'\\\\'',[('\\\\''v41'\\\\'',9071)],'\\\\''E'\\\\'')]:\n f=p.pair_family(draw,*calls) if not keys else {'\\\\''members'\\\\'': {calls[0][0]:{'\\\\''what'\\\\'': p.W(*next(v[4] for v in p.SINGLETONS if v[0]==keys)), '\\\\''bands'\\\\'':p.bands(draw,calls[0][0])}}, '\\\\''relations'\\\\'':[],'\\\\''shared'\\\\'':[]}\n if keys=='\\\\''S'\\\\'':f['\\\\''members'\\\\'']['\\\\''v6'\\\\'']['\\\\''what'\\\\'']['\\\\''period'\\\\'']='\\\\''CY2026'\\\\''\n f=p.small_family(f,p.PAIR_SCOPES if not keys else (),{'\\\\''v29'\\\\'':p.O_NOTE} if keys=='\\\\''O'\\\\'' else None)\n x=p.item(keys or '\\\\''P'\\\\'','\\\\''joint'\\\\'' if not keys else '\\\\''single'\\\\'',draw,calls,f,[v for v,_ in calls],'\\\\''v13s'\\\\'')\n print('\\\\''blind'\\\\'',keys or '\\\\''P'\\\\'',len(x['\\\\''shown'\\\\'']),len(x['\\\\''passages'\\\\'']),x['\\\\''questions'\\\\''],[(v,k['\\\\''bands'\\\\'']) for v,k in f['\\\\''members'\\\\''].items()])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"pair-old-1 e2652 'Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.'\npair-old-2 e2497 'NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.'\npair-old-2 e4680 'For the current quarter, CEO Jensen Huang’s firm projected revenue of $108.0 billion (+/-2%) vs. consensus for $104.6 billion. That would be good for growth of roughly 90% and Nvidia Is known for beating its guidance.'\npair-old-2 e4704 'Three direct customers generated 44% ($78.2 billion) of Nvidia’s $177.8 billion revenue in the first half of fiscal 2027—up from two customers driving 35% a year earlier.'\npair-old-2 e4761 'However, I think Nvidia could report third-quarter revenue of around $113 billion to $114 billion.'\npair-old-2 e4963 'Rotating chairman Eric Xu said the company therefore has no plans for a large-scale overseas expansion for now.'\npair-old-3 e2754 'Revenue\\n$\\n96,221\\n$\\n46,743\\n$\\n177,837\\n$\\n90,805'\npair-old-3 e4867 \"Most of those chips are Nvidia's.\"\nsingle-O e4648 'Nvidia could invest as much as $10 billion'\nsingle-S e2489 'U.S. hyperscalers are expected to spend roughly $916 billion on capital expenditures over the next 12 months, with consensus estimates projecting that figure to rise to nearly $1.2 trillion the year after.'\nsingle-S e4867 'The company also guided for gross margins of between 72% and 73% in its fiscal 2028.'\nsingle-E e3660 'The bad news for AMD and Intel is that Kress said Nvidia not only still expects $20 billion in CPU revenue in its fiscal 2027, but expects that number to more than double in fiscal 2028.'\nblind P 296 296 {'v4': {'question': \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\", 'ladder': ['Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion.', 'Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion.', 'Total revenue is at least $352.8 billion and below $392 billion.', 'Total revenue is at least $313.6 billion and below $352.8 billion.', 'Total revenue is below $313.6 billion.']}, 'v8': {'question': 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'ladder': ['FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $400 billion.', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion.', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $300 billion and less than $350 billion.', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $300 billion.', 'FY2027 Data Center revenue is less than $250 billion.']}} [('v4', [[431.2, None], [392.0, 431.2], [352.8, 392.0], [313.6, 352.8], [None, 313.6]]), ('v8', [[400.0, None], [350.0, 400.0], [300.0, 350.0], [250.0, 300.0], [None, 250.0]])]\nblind S 50 50 {'v6': {'question': 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?', 'ladder': ['Combined spending is below $500 billion.', 'Combined spending is at least $500 billion and below $600 billion.', 'Combined spending is at least $600 billion and below $700 billion.', 'Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $800 billion.', 'Combined spending is at least $800 billion.']}} [('v6', [[None, 500.0], [500.0, 600.0], [600.0, 700.0], [700.0, 800.0], [800.0, None]])]\nblind O 30 30 {'v29': {'question': \"How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\", 'ladder': ['Commitments are below $25 billion.', 'Commitments are at least $25 billion and below $50 billion.', 'Commitments are at least $50 billion and below $75 billion.', 'Commitments are at least $75 billion and below $100 billion.', 'Commitments are at least $100 billion.']}} [('v29', [[None, 25.0], [25.0, 50.0], [50.0, 75.0], [75.0, 100.0], [100.0, None]])]\nblind E 15 15 {'v41': {'question': 'What will NVIDIA report as Vera CPU revenue for FY2028?', 'ladder': ['FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is at least $50 billion.', 'FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is at least $40 billion and less than $50 billion.', 'FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is at least $30 billion and less than $40 billion.', 'FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is at least $20 billion and less than $30 billion.', 'FY2028 Vera CPU revenue is less than $20 billion.']}} [('v41', [[50.0, None], [40.0, 50.0], [30.0, 40.0], [20.0, 30.0], [None, 20.0]])]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,copy,math\nsys.path[:0]=['\\\\''docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers'\\\\'','\\\\''src'\\\\'']\nimport paid_gate as p, small_cases as sc, calc_small as c\nF,A,W=sc.F,sc.A,sc.W\nP={(i['\\\\''unit'\\\\''],i['\\\\''arm'\\\\'']):i for i in p.build_plan('\\\\''v13s'\\\\'')}\ndef check(label,it,fs,ans):\n a={'\\\\''figures'\\\\'':fs,'\\\\''answers'\\\\'':ans}\n se=p.model.check_schema(a,it['\\\\''schema'\\\\''])\n if se:\n  print(label,'\\\\''SCHEMA'\\\\'',str(se[0])[:220]); return\n v=c.from_answer(a,it['\\\\''family'\\\\''])\n try:\n  r=c.check(it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],it['\\\\''passages'\\\\''],v)\n  print(label, '\\\\''schema=[]'\\\\'', '\\\\''decode='\\\\'',v['\\\\''decode_errors'\\\\''],'\\\\''check='\\\\'',r['\\\\''errors'\\\\''],'\\\\''publication='\\\\'',c.publish_decision(it['\\\\''family'\\\\''],v,r),'\\\\''values='\\\\'',r['\\\\''published'\\\\''])\n except Exception as ex: print(label,'\\\\''schema=[]'\\\\'','\\\\''decode='\\\\'',v['\\\\''decode_errors'\\\\''],'\\\\''EXCEPTION'\\\\'',type(ex).__name__,str(ex))\n return v\ndef one(it,fs,**kw):\n v=it['\\\\''members'\\\\''][0]; m=it['\\\\''family'\\\\'']['\\\\''members'\\\\''][v]\n rung=kw.pop('\\\\''rung'\\\\'',2); value=kw.pop('\\\\''value'\\\\'',400)\n return [*fs,F('\\\\''OUT'\\\\'',m['\\\\''what'\\\\''],'\\\\''estimate'\\\\'','\\\\''forecast'\\\\'','\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',value=value, basis_text='\\\\''Evidence and assumptions as above'\\\\'', outcome_for=[v],**kw)], [A(v,rung=rung,reference_unavailable='\\\\''No directly comparable market figure'\\\\'')]\nit=P['\\\\''pair-old-1'\\\\'','\\\\''separate-v4'\\\\'']\ndef source(fid,what,e,t,value=None,unit='\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',q='\\\\''none'\\\\'',basis='\\\\''reported'\\\\'',**kw):\n return F(fid,what,'\\\\''source'\\\\'',basis,unit,value=value,evidence_id=e,quote_number=t,qualifier=q,**kw)\ndef comp(fid,what,op,inputs,value=None,basis='\\\\''reported'\\\\'',unit='\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',**kw):\n return F(fid,what,'\\\\''computed'\\\\'',basis,unit,operation=op,inputs=inputs,value=value,**kw)\ndef est(fid,what,value=None,basis='\\\\''forecast'\\\\'',**kw):\n return F(fid,what,'\\\\''estimate'\\\\'',basis,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'',value=value,basis_text='\\\\''From guidance and past results'\\\\'',**kw)\ndef wp(t):return W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027'\\\\''+('\\\\'' '\\\\''+t if t else '\\\\'''\\\\''))\ndef dp(t):return W('\\\\''Data Center'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027'\\\\''+('\\\\'' '\\\\''+t if t else '\\\\'''\\\\''))\nbase=[\n source('\\\\''Q1'\\\\'',wp('\\\\''Q1'\\\\''),'\\\\''e111'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$81.62 billion'\"'\\\\'',81.62),\n source('\\\\''Q2'\\\\'',wp('\\\\''Q2'\\\\''),'\\\\''e2649'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$96.2 billion'\"'\\\\'',96.2),\n source('\\\\''T'\\\\'',wp('\\\\''Q3'\\\\''),'\\\\''e5056'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$113.6 billion'\"'\\\\'',113.6,q='\\\\''roughly'\\\\'',basis='\\\\''third_party'\\\\''),\n est('\\\\''Q3'\\\\'',wp('\\\\''Q3'\\\\''),113.6,rests_on=['\\\\''T'\\\\'']),\n source('\\\\''LY'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2026 Q4'\\\\''),'\\\\''e2452'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$68 billion'\"'\\\\'',68),\n source('\\\\''YG'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q4'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''year-over-year growth'\\\\''),'\\\\''e5162'\\\\'','\\\\''65%'\\\\'',65,unit='\\\\''%'\\\\'',basis='\\\\''third_party'\\\\''),\n comp('\\\\''Q4'\\\\'',wp('\\\\''Q4'\\\\''),'\\\\''apply_growth'\\\\'',['\\\\''LY'\\\\'','\\\\''YG'\\\\''],112.2,basis='\\\\''forecast'\\\\''),\n source('\\\\''MR'\\\\'',wp('\\\\'''\\\\''),'\\\\''e5204'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$411 billion'\"'\\\\'',411,basis='\\\\''consensus'\\\\'',reference_for=['\\\\''v4'\\\\'']),\n comp('\\\\''FY'\\\\'',wp('\\\\'''\\\\''),'\\\\''sum'\\\\'',['\\\\''Q1'\\\\'','\\\\''Q2'\\\\'','\\\\''Q3'\\\\'','\\\\''Q4'\\\\''],403.62,basis='\\\\''forecast'\\\\'',outcome_for=['\\\\''v4'\\\\'']),\n]\nans=[A('\\\\''v4'\\\\'',rung=2)]\ndef pos(n,fs):\n return next(f for f in fs if f['\\\\''id'\\\\'']==n)\ncheck('\\\\''line 4 converted control'\\\\'',it,base,ans)\n\nfor name,e,quote,val,unit,qual,extra in [\n ('\\\\''S1 5% cut from 85%'\\\\'','\\\\''e111'\\\\'','\\\\''5%'\\\\'',5,'\\\\''%'\\\\'', '\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''S1 plus or minus fragment as +2%'\\\\'', '\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''2%'\\\\'',2,'\\\\''%'\\\\'', '\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''S1 plus or minus fragment as exact \"'$108B'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$108.0 billion'\"'\\\\'',108,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''S1 dropped scale and digit'\\\\'','\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$108'\"'\\\\'',108/1e9,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''S1 dropped range endpoint'\\\\'','\\\\''e3346'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$105.84 billion'\"'\\\\'',105.84,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''S1 compound range control'\\\\'','\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%'\"'\\\\'',None,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{'\\\\''low'\\\\'':105.84,'\\\\''high'\\\\'':110.16}),\n ('\\\\''S1 supposed upper bound accepted as point'\\\\'','\\\\''e5056'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$113.6 billion'\"'\\\\'',113.6,'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{}),\n ('\\\\''nonfinite as source'\\\\'','\\\\''e2652'\\\\'','\\\\''\"'$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%'\"'\\\\'',float('\\\\''inf'\\\\''),'\\\\''USD bn'\\\\'','\\\\''none'\\\\'',{})\n]:\n f=source('\\\\''EX'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2027 Q3'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''test quote'\\\\''),e,quote,val,unit,qual,**extra)\n check(name,it,[*base,f],ans)\ni=P['\\\\''single-S'\\\\'','\\\\''single'\\\\'']\ns=source('\\\\''G'\\\\'',W('\\\\''company'\\\\'','\\\\''FY2028'\\\\'',measure='\\\\''gross margin'\\\\''), '\\\\''e4867'\\\\'','\\\\''between 72% and 73%'\\\\'',unit='\\\\''%'\\\\'',basis='\\\\''guidance'\\\\'',low=72,high=73)\ncheck('\\\\''right S1 written percentage range'\\\\'',i,*one(i,[s],value=1110,rung=5,rests_on=['\\\\''G'\\\\'']))\ni=P['\\\\''pair-old