{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready.** v13s accepts `5%` copied out of `85%`, refuses a correct $411 billion calculation, and publishes an impossible range for the same calculation. The blind test also accepts altered first replies and can finish preparing packets with zero replies.\n\nI rebuilt all 12 gate requests and reviewed the 36 stored first replies. I ran the examples below through `model.check_schema`, `from_answer`, and `check` in memory, including both separate replies before and after joining them. I reproduced the 80 case passes, all 28 mutation results, and the old v13 request plan and `results.json` byte for byte. I reviewed the saved A4 rehearsal and reproduced the relevant reconciliation and card paths in memory. The full A4 script requires a writable folder.\n\n## High severity\n\n1. **S1 accepts fragments as complete numbers (a), (d).** The request says “the number exactly as the quote writes it” and “a written range in full.” The checker finds substrings and only checks for an immediately preceding dash. In the actual gate passages, it accepted `5%` from `85%` (`e111`), `2%` as a positive rate and `$108.0 billion` as a standalone point from `$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%` (`e2652`), and `$105.84 billion` alone from the written range in `e3346`. The complete expressions passed as controls. [calc_small.py:345](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:345) · [render_v13.py:103](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:103)\n\n2. **S2 gives one uncertain number different values along different paths (a), (c), (d).** The request says “compute both extremes, a figure used twice taking one value.” Using the stored revenue inputs, I subtracted the first three quarters from $411B to get Q4, then added those same quarters back. The checker refused the exact answer, accepted `$406.68B–$415.32B`, and published that spread when I declared the permitted midpoint of $411B. It keeps one value per immediate input ID but loses that link across intermediate figures. Testing only endpoints also gives `[-2, 3] × itself = [4, 9]`. The correct range is `[0, 9]`, which it refused. [calc_small.py:207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:207) · [calc_small.py:391](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:391) · [render_v13.py:116](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:116)\n\n3. **S3 skips a part above its whole and compares the wrong ends of linked ranges (a), (d).** The header requires a comparison for every listed quarter and paired ends when the part is calculated from the whole. After joining the separate replies, Q3 Data Center at $120B against company revenue of $113.6B was refused. Adding an unused $105B Data Center alternative made the same calculation publish because the checker skipped the quarter. In a second answer, `part = 215 − whole` passed for a whole of `$105.84B–$110.16B`. At the whole’s low end the part is $109.16B. Comparing the two sorted ranges hides that violation. [calc_small.py:521](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:521) · [render_v13.py:157](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:157)\n\n4. **S8 rejects a correct sum across separate periods and accepts wrong period arithmetic (a), (c), (d).** Using the old-1 reply’s inputs, `$177.82B` of company revenue in H1 plus `$105.08B` of Data Center revenue in Q3 gives a valid `$282.90B` floor through Q3. S8 refused it as double-counting. The periods do not overlap. The checker also accepted company Q3 minus Data Center Q2 as the Q3 remainder, even though the request says a difference must “give the rest.” Finally, it refused a correctly calculated H1 with the plain-English output label, as the request’s spelling rule requires, but accepted Q1 + Q2 + Q2 as H1 when all three period labels were plain English. [calc_small.py:546](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:546) · [render_v13.py:118](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:118)\n\n5. **S4 refuses two agreeing separate replies after joining them (c), (d).** I translated the stored v4 and v8 replies into v13s. Both published, and their matching Q3 and Q4 figures joined successfully. I then wrote each reply’s use of the same cited 65% Q4 growth assumption as its own forecast figure. Both replies still published individually, with the same results. After joining, S4 refused the pair because both copies of the 65% figure remained, although one was no longer used. Joining combines matching figures only for the listed shared quantities, while S4 counts every forecast, including unused ones. The request also says “compute each quantity and period once,” which is broader than D738’s restriction on forecast figures and its allowance for competing outside inputs. [answers.jsonl:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl:4) · [paid_gate.py:376](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid_gate.py:376) · [calc_small.py:475](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:475) · [render_v13.py:148](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:148)\n\n6. **The blind runner can produce a result from the wrong material (e).** All six registered requests built successfully, including the expected 79 fresh quotes for P and 41 for S. The reader packet contains the whole raw reply and all shown passages. However, the checker extracts the text between the outermost braces, so it accepted a reply with a prose preface and also accepts an object wrapped in an array. I ran `check` and `packets` with zero writer replies and both completed successfully. There is no enforcement of two designated replies per case, 24 readings, or the required third readings. Reversing S’s ladder also passed the builder because it compares sorted edges. The review needs an explicit outcome for an unresolved singleton and an accepted reply with broken structure. [blind_test.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:64) · [blind_test.py:105](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:105) · [blind_test.py:139](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:139) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:244](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:244)\n\n## Remaining rule gaps\n\n| Rule | Confirmed gap |\n|---|---|\n| **S1 (c), (d)** | The request says “a written range in full,” but the full `between 72% and 73%` in S passage `e4867` fails. “As much as $10 billion” in O passage `e4648` has no valid qualifier spelling. `none` passes and drops the cap. The stored old-3 reply also correctly reads `$177.837B` from `e2754`, but the shown table cell has no scale. The literal cell is read as `0.000177837 USD bn`, and the correctly scaled summary is refused because it is outside the quote. That last case is a gap in what the request supplies. [calc_small.py:19](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:19) · [calc_small.py:378](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:378) · [render_v13.py:103](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:103) · [answers.jsonl:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13-paid-gate-2026-11-22/answers.jsonl:16) |\n| **S2 (c), (d)** | The stated ratio units allow equal units or USD bn divided by `x`. The checker also accepts `% ÷ x`. The stated `share` operation takes the whole’s unit and a 0–100 percent input, but the checker refuses `25% of 40% = 10%` solely because the whole is a percentage. [calc_small.py:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:167) · [render_v13.py:111](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:111) |\n| **S4 (c), (d)** | In a control where the outcome itself is a listed shared quantity, the checker refuses guidance reached through that very outcome forecast. The header says to go through the forecast. The walk skips applying that rule to the outcome itself. The current gate has no such member. [calc_small.py:484](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:484) · [render_v13.py:168](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:168) |\n| **S5 (b), (d)** | The request says `reference_unavailable` is used “when no figure is marked.” An empty string alongside a marked reference passes. It also says `rests_on` is estimate-only. Attaching an outside source to a reported figure through that forbidden field made an otherwise refused reported-only market reference pass. [calc_small.py:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:144) · [calc_small.py:463](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:463) · [render_v13.py:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:124) |\n| **S6 (b), (d)** | The request requires a range’s rung to have a reason “in reasons,” but an empty reason publishes. It also fails to say explicitly that the rung is checked against the recomputed range or point, which can differ from the declared number within tolerance. [calc_small.py:455](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:455) · [render_v13.py:137](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:137) |\n| **S7 (b), (d)** | An unresolved answer with `reference_unavailable: \"\"` passes despite the required null. An estimate with `inputs: [\"NO_FIGURE\"]` also passes despite “Computed only: ids of figures, never passages.” A forecast carrying `why` passes despite “Unresolved only.” Separately, a schema-valid 401-digit integer raises `OverflowError`, and JSON `1e400` turns into infinity and passes S1 as the value of `$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%`. The blind runner does not handle the checker exception per reply. [calc_small.py:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:145) · [calc_small.py:234](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:234) · [calc_small.py:294](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_small.py:294) · [render_v13.py:110](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:110) · [blind_test.py:125](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_test.py:125) |\n\n## Cases and mutants\n\n- **Registered cases (e).** A1 still asks for two sources for `±` guidance, while D738 and the request require one complete source. The A2 case labelled “Data Center × 1x added to company” never performs the addition. The registered case that copies `2%` out of `plus or minus 2%` is absent. The existing case changes the declared midpoint while leaving the quote intact. The assertion checks for any message with the expected rule code, while the registration calls for the intended message as well. [SMALL-DESIGN.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:173) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:215](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:215) · [small_cases.py:324](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:324) · [small_cases.py:382](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:382) · [small_cases.py:477](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_cases.py:477)\n- **Mutants and A4 (e).** All 28 mutations produced a failing assertion in memory. Several fixtures still refused the mutated answer for another reason. For example, disabling the S5 forecast-reference check leaves an S4 duplicate, and disabling the S8 part-plus-whole check also leaves an S4 duplicate. Those tests show the intended error disappeared. They do not show that it independently prevented publication. The mutation runner can also report a crashing control as passing. A4 tests S3 and S4 refusals plus an invalid rung, while its registration requires a defective and correct pair for each of the five named defects. [small_mutants.py:70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_mutants.py:70) · [small-mutants.log:14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small-mutants.log:14) · [small_rehearsal.py:159](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/small_rehearsal.py:159) · [SMALL-DESIGN.md:240](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:240)\n\nBefore opening the blind test, rerun A4 with these counterexamples paired with their correct versions, and require the blind runner to reject altered replies and incomplete inventories."}}
